Jayka in [[Stonetalon Mountains]]\r\n* Innkeeper Fizzgrimble in [[Tanaris]]\r\n* Innkeeper Shyria in [[Feralas]]\r\n* Innkeeper Greul in [[Feralas]]\r\n* Innkeeper Thulfram in [[The Hinterlands]]\r\n* Mardrack Greenwell in [[Feralas]]\r\n* Faralorn in [[Feralas]]\r\n* Harklane in [[Feralas]]\r\n* Dirge Quikcleave in [[Tanaris]]\r\n* Gikkix in [[Tanaris]]\r\n* Jabbey in [[Tanaris]]\r\n* Loorana in [[Feralas]]\r\n* Janet Hommers in [[Desolace]]\r\n* Harnor in [[Desolace]]\r\n* Kuruk in [[Mulgore]]\r\n* Innkeeper Heather in [[Westfall]]\r\n* Innkeeper Shul'kar in [[Badlands]]\r\n* Innkeeper Adegwa in [[Arathi Highlands]]\r\n* Shrye Ragefist in [[Alterac Valley]]\r\n* Caretaker Alen in [[Eastern Plaguelands]]\r\n* Innkeeper Lyshaerya in [[Desolace]]\r\n* Innkeeper Sikewa in [[Desolace]]\r\n* Innkeeper Abeqwa in [[Thousand Needles]]\r\n* Innkeeper Vizzie in [[Winterspring]]\r\n* Himmik in [[Winterspring]]\r\n* Baker Masterson in [[Western Plaguelands]]\r\n* Gorn One Eye in [[Felwood]]\r\n* Dargon in [[Moonglade]]\r\n* Daeolyn Summerleaf in [[Moonglade]]\r\n* My'lanna in [[Moonglade]]\r\n* Tukk in [[Desolace]]\r\n* Stormpike Quartermaster in [[Alterac Valley]]\r\n* Frostwolf Quartermaster in [[Alterac Valley]]\r\n* Innkeeper Kaylisk in [[Ashenvale]]\r\n* Super-Seller 680 in [[Desolace]]\r\n* Nergal in [[Un'Goro Crater]]\r\n* Christi Galvanis in [[Desolace]]\r\n* Shen'dralar Provisioner in [[Dire Maul]]\r\n* Master Smith Burninate in [[Searing Gorge]]\r\n* Lard in [[The Hinterlands]]\r\n* Gapp Jinglepocket in [[Ashenvale]]\r\n* Hecht Copperpinch in [[The Barrens]]\r\n* Targot Jinglepocket in [[Arathi Highlands]]\r\n* Kosco Copperpinch in [[Arathi Highlands]]\r\n* Calandrath in [[Silithus]]\r\n* Marniel Amberlight in [[Eversong Woods]]\r\n* Innkeeper Delaniel in [[Eversong Woods]]\r\n* Sathren Azuredawn in [[Silvermoon City]]\r\n* Jessica Chambers in [[Eastern Plaguelands]]\r\n* Zalene Firstlight in [[Eversong Woods]]\r\n* Innkeeper Faralia in [[Stonetalon Mountains]]\r\n* Innkeeper Kalarin in [[Ghostlands]]\r\n* Caregiver Chellan in [[Azuremyst Isle]]\r\n* Innkeeper Velandra in [[Silvermoon City]]\r\n* Onnis in [[The Exodar]]\r\n* Caregiver Breel in [[The Exodar]]\r\n* Caregiver Topher Loaal in [[Bloodmyst Isle]]\r\n* Innkeeper Jovia in [[Silvermoon City]]\r\n* Heron Skygaze in [[Ghostlands]]\r\n* Shaarubo in [[Shattrath City]]\r\n* Boots in [[Netherstorm]]\r\n* Little Azimi in [[Bloodmyst Isle]]\r\nThis item can be looted from most level 40-57 [[Humanoid]] monsters.\r\nThis item can also be found in [[Box of Rations]]",},
			["Moonbrook"] = { content = "'''Moonbrook''' is a [[Defias Brotherhood]] controlled ghost town southwest of [[Sentinel Hill]].\r\n==Destruction and Reconstruction==\r\nPrior to the coming of the [[orcs]] to [[Azeroth]], Moonbrook served as the focal point of the farmlands of [[Westfall]]. During the [[First War]], Moonbrook and its sister town [[Goldshire]] were the final two towns to fall to the [[Horde]] prior to the razing of [[Stormwind Keep]]. It was rebuilt following the [[Alliance]] victory in the [[Second War]].\r\n==The Defias==\r\nFollowing successful efforts by the Defias to seize control of Westfall, Moonbrook was abandoned. It is currently controlled by the Defias, and is used by them to access their main base of operations, the [[Deadmines]].\r\n==A Town in WoW==\r\nIn Westfall, a town arrow will point to Moonbrook. This is because there is a freewheeling merchant in one of the buildings that is friendly to all players, regardless of faction, that serves as a repairer and general goods vendor to players who are brave or foolish enough to venture into the [[Deadmines]]. He may also make Moonbrook the only [[Horde]]-friendly outpost near [[Stormwind]].",},
			["Mooncloth"] = { content = "'''Mooncloth''' is a magical [[cloth]], imbued with the power of the [[Moonwell]]s.\r\n==Source==\r\nPurifying '''Mooncloth''' requires 250 skill in [[Tailoring]] and can be learned from a pattern which can be bought from [[Qia]] (limited supply) in [[Everlook]]. The procedure requires 2x Felcloth, must be performed near a [[Moonwell]] (even corrupted moonwells in [[Felwood]] will do).\r\n==Mooncloth as an Ingredient==\r\n'''Mooncloth''' is used in the following recipes\r\n===[[Leatherworking]]===\r\n*Living Breastplate\r\n====Armor====\r\n*Belt of the Archmage\r\n*Flarecore Leggings\r\n*Flarecore Robe\r\n*Flarecore Wraps\r\n*Gloves of Spell Mastery\r\n*Truefaith Vestments\r\n*Argent Shoulders\r\n*Bloodvine Boots\r\n*Bloodvine Leggings\r\n*Bloodvine Vest\r\n*Gaea's Embrace\r\n*Mantle of the Timbermaw\r\n*Mooncloth Boots\r\n*Mooncloth Circlet\r\n*Mooncloth Gloves\r\n*Mooncloth Leggings\r\n*Mooncloth Robe\r\n*Mooncloth Shoulders\r\n*Mooncloth Vest\r\n*Sylvan Crown\r\n====Bags====\r\n*Satchel of Cenarius\r\n*Mooncloth Bag\r\n*Bottomless Bag\r\n==Mooncloth as a Quest Objective==\r\n*Sacred Cloth\r\n*Anthion's Strange Request\r\n*Uniform Supplies",},
			["Mooncloth Bag"] = { content = "'''Mooncloth Bag''' is a 16 slot bag made from [[Mooncloth]]. It ties with the [[Traveler's Backpack]] as the largest bag that does not bind (either when picked up or when used).\r\n==Source==\r\nThis item is crafted by [[Tailoring|Tailors]] with a skill level of 300.\r\nThe components are:\r\n*4 [[Bolt of Runecloth|Bolts of Runecloth]]\r\n*1 [[Mooncloth]]\r\n*1 [[Rune Thread]]\r\nThe [[pattern]] is a [[World Drop]].",},
			["Mooncloth Boots"] = { content = "==Source==\r\n'''Mooncloth Boots''' are crafted by [[Tailoring|Tailors]] with a skill level of 290.\r\nThe components are:\r\n*6 Bolt of Runecloth\r\n*4 Mooncloth\r\n*2 Black Pearl\r\n*1 Rune Thread\r\nThe [[pattern]] is a quest reward for completing the quest [[Quest:Sacred Cloth|Sacred Cloth]] given by [[Meilosh]] in the [[Timbermaw Hold]] in [[Felwood]]. You need to have Friendly reputation for the [[Timbermaw Furbolgs]] and must have a [[Tailoring]] skill of 290.",},
			["Mooncloth Circlet"] = { content = "'''Mooncloth Circlet''' is a good replacement to [[Tier 0]] armor set for cloth wearers.\r\n==Source==\r\nMooncloth Circlet is crafted by [[Tailoring|Tailors]] with a skill level of 300.\r\nThe components are:\r\n*4 [[Bolt of Runecloth|Bolts of Runecloth]]\r\n*6 [[Mooncloth]]\r\n*1 [[Azerothian Diamond]]\r\n*2 [[Enchanted Leather]]s\r\n*2 [[Rune Thread]]s\r\nThe [[pattern]] is a [[World Drop]].",},
			["Mooncloth Gloves"] = { content = "==Source==\r\nThis item can be crafted using [[Tailoring]] (300); taught by Pattern: Mooncloth Gloves.",},
			["Mooncloth Leggings"] = { content = "'''Mooncloth Leggings''' is cloth leg armor, usefull to Priests, Mages and Warlocks until they find [[Dungeon Set 1|Tier 0]] gear.\r\n==Source==\r\nMooncloth Leggings is crafted by [[Tailoring|Tailors]] with a skill level of 290.\r\nThe components are:\r\n*6 [[Bolt of Runecloth]]\r\n*4 [[Mooncloth]]\r\n*1 [[Rune Thread]]\r\nThe [[pattern]] is a world drop.",},
			["Mooncloth Robe"] = { content = "==Source==\r\nThis item can be crafted using [[Tailoring]] (300); taught by Pattern: Mooncloth Robe.",},
			["Mooncloth Shoulders"] = { content = "==Source==\r\nThis item can be crafted using [[Tailoring]] (300); taught by Pattern: Mooncloth Shoulders.",},
			["Mooncloth Tailoring"] = { content = "'''Primal Mooncloth Tailoring''' is one of the [[Tailoring]] Specializations you are able to choose in [[Shattrath City]].\r\nPrimal Mooncloth Specialization allows you to create two units of [[Primal Mooncloth]] instead of one using the same amount of materials and grants access to specific tailoring recipes.\r\n==Becoming a Mooncloth Tailor==\r\nTo specialize in Primal Mooncloth Tailoring, a tailor must complete Becoming a Mooncloth Tailor, given by Nasmara Moonsong in [[Shattrath City]]. To obtain this quest you need to have 350 proficency in Tailoring. While you can learn 350 Tailoring as early as level 50, the quest requires at least level 60.\r\nTo complete the quest, travel to the [[Moonwell]] located at Cenarion Refuge in [[Zangarmarsh]] and use the provided quest item, then travel back to Shattrath City to complete the quest. \r\nEarier entries stating that this quest can be completed at any [[Moonwell]] are incorrect. The Sample piece of cloth clearly states in the item tool tip to go to Zangarmarsh. Any attempt to craft the sample at another [[Moonwell]] will result in an error message. \r\nYou don't need any mats to complete the quest, and it won't start the cooldown on Primal Mooncloth crafting. Immediately after completing the quest you may travel back to the moonwell to craft your first two pieces of Primal Mooncloth.\r\n===Changing Specialization===\r\nSince patch [[2.1.0]], you may now re-specialize. It will cost 150 gold to unlearn the current specialization.\r\n==Crafting Primal Mooncloth==\r\nCrafting Primal Mooncloth is not exclusive to Primal Mooncloth tailors, but the specialization will always produce 2 pieces of Primal Mooncloth with the mats for a single one.\r\nThe materials are:\r\nA tailor must be in any Moonwell area to craft Primal Mooncloth. The cooldown on the crafting is 96 hours (4 days), but it's not shared with the cooldowns on the other types of specialized cloth, namely [[Spellcloth]] and [[Shadowcloth]].\r\n==Exclusive Patterns==\r\nPrimal Mooncloth Tailoring gives exclusive access to the following patterns:\r\n*Primal Mooncloth Belt\r\n*Primal Mooncloth Shoulders\r\n*Primal Mooncloth Robe\r\nThese patterns require the specialization to be obtained, and the items are Bind on Pickup, meaning only Primal Mooncloth Tailors could ever have the crafted items.\r\nThe Primal Mooncloth Set is arguably the best Holy [[Priest]] equipment attainable before the 25-man raid instances. It nicely complements the Whitemend Set (Whitemend Hood & Whitemend Pants), because it uses different equipment slots.\r\n===Material cost to construct set===\r\nTo make the complete set you'll need:",},
			["Mooncloth Vest"] = { content = "'''Mooncloth Vest''' is cloth chest armor, useful to Priests, Mages and Warlocks until they find their [[Tier 0]] chest or better.\r\n=Source=\r\nMooncloth Vest is crafted by [[Tailoring|Tailors]] with a skill level of 300.\r\nThe components are:\r\n*6 [[Bolt of Runecloth]]\r\n*4 [[Mooncloth]]\r\n*1 [[Rune Thread]]\r\nThe [[pattern]] is a world drop.\r\n=Notes=",},
			["Mooncrystal"] = { content = "Cut from the emerald Eye of Jennala, it opens the mind of the Gate Keeper.\r\n==Notes==\r\nThe three Mooncrystals form the [[Key of the Three Moons (item)|Key of the Three Moons]], while two of them create a [[Partial Key of the Three Moons]].",},
			["Moonfire"] = { content = "'''Moonfire''' is an [[instant]] [[Hybrid spell|hybrid]] spell used by [[Druid]]s.\r\n==Notes==\r\n* Does less [[Direct Damage]] than [[Wrath]], but is an [[instant]] cast and does [[Damage over Time|DoT]].\r\n* The rank 12 Moonfire gets +spell damage from gear per following formula:\r\nDD part = Spell Dmg * 34.7% * 1.5 / 3.5 (14.87%)\r\nDoT Part = Spell Dmg * 65.3% * 12 / 15 (52.24%)\r\n67.11% total\r\n==Tips and tactics==\r\n*Use after the pull, at the beginning of a battle. That way the [[Damage over Time|DoT]] will take its effect.\r\n*Also great for tagging during a time-critical pull, such as when the mob is in danger of walking away or being tagged by another group. Unlike ranged weapons, the damage occurs as soon as the spell is cast.\r\n*It is better to use [[Wrath]] or [[Starfire]] when in a group (after you cast Moonfire once), as you can afford to take time to cast it.\r\n*The first rank of Moonfire is a great way to destroy totems without using much mana or having to move into enemies while healing.\r\n*The [[Damage over Time|DoT]] of the highest rank will always tick and will not be removed by casting a lower rank of Moonfire on that target. So it is possible to spam Moonfire rank 11 while the DoT of rank 12 continues to tick.",},
			["Moonfury"] = { content = "==Functionality==\r\nPure increase to damage done with the druid's primary offensive spells.\r\n==Notes==\r\n*Not a giant burst damage increase, however does result in an overall increase in DPS.\r\n*This effect is added to the bonus from [[Improved Moonfire]] so that fully talented, [[Moonfire]] damage is increased by 20%.\r\n*This effect is multiplied by the bonus from [[Wrath of Cenarius]]. The fully talented effective [[Spell damage coefficient]] for [[Starfire]] becomes 132% (1.1*1.2).\r\n*Base damage for Wrath/Starfire (as reported by in-game tooltip) goes up by slightly more than the expected amount. At 5/5 Moonfury, The Wrath damage range changes from (381-429) to (422-475) and SF range changes from (540-636) to (605-711).",},
			["Moonglade"] = { content = "The '''Moonglade''' (also spelled '''Moonglades''' and '''Moon Glade''') is a vale in [[Northern Kalimdor]] that serves as a haven for [[druid]]s, and is also the home of the [[Cenarion Circle]]. Here, [[tauren]] and [[night elf|night elves]] coexist peacefully, united by their reverence for the spirit of [[nature]]. Conflict between the races in Moonglade is not tolerated by the [[Moonglade Warden]]s stationed throughout the main town of [[Nighthaven]], who will respond to any violence initiated against individuals with a favorable reputation with the Circle.\r\nMoonglade's reflection within the [[Emerald Dream]] is the most sacred place in the entire realm. The [[Rift of Aln]] is located here in [[Lake Elune'ara]]'s place.\r\nThe [[demigod]] [[Omen]] sleeps at the depths of the central lake, awakening every year around the time of the [[Lunar Festival]], after which he is routinely put to rest. The Lunar Festival itself is also based in Nighthaven. The [[Moonkin Festival]] also occurs in the area.\r\n==History==\r\nAround the time of the [[War of the Ancients]], Cenarius dwelled within the sacred Moonglade. As the war on [[Kalimdor (landmass)|Kalimdor]] progressed and the [[Burning Legion|Legion's]] numbers swelled, [[Malfurion Stormrage]] realized that the [[Night elf|night elves]] could not prevail alone. He convinced [[Tyrande Whisperwind]] and his brother [[Illidan Stormrage|Illidan]] to accompany him to the tranquil Moonglade. They beseeched Cenarius for aid. Following the Great Sundering, the [[Keeper of the grove|keepers of the grove]] and [[dryad]]s emerged from the secluded Moonglade and ventured into the world. Moonglade was considered sacred for [[night elf]] druids, with kaldorei society devoting itself more to nature worship and protection. Cenarius himself has remained here.\r\nDuring the [[War of the Satyr]], [[Malfurion Stormrage]] called several druids to here to establish a new druid organization called the [[Cenarion Circle]] in order to fight the [[Druids of the Scythe]].\r\nDuring the [[Third War]], a [[Scourge]] force led by [[Tichondrius]] laid waste to the woods near the [[Stormrage Barrow Dens]] trying to get to Malfurion's body. Arriving near the [[Moonglade Isle]], [[Tyrande Whisperwind]], her [[Sentinel]]s and several dryads fought against a [[Horde]] base and the [[Primal Guardians|isle guardians]] and retrieved the [[Horn of Cenarius]] which she used to wake Malfurion from his slumber. Despite the Scourge presence, the land of the Moonglade was not shown to have been befouled.\r\nYears after the Third War, Moonglade was opened to all druid races. [[Keeper Remulos]] became Moonglade's new guardian.\r\nMore recently, the peace in Moonglade itself has become threatened as bizarre creatures from the [[Emerald Nightmare]] have found a way into a wing of the Stormrage Barrow Dens.\r\nDuring the [[War Against the Nightmare]], the Moonglade was wholly shrouded in dark mist, giving it more the appearance of a graveyard. For a brief time, [[Hamuul Runetotem]] taught [[Lucan Foxblood]] how to control his unique abilities here.\r\nShortly before the Cataclysm, after [[Magatha Grimtotem]] usurped the tauren leadership, the tauren of the druidic stronghold Moonglade began their rebellion, and false rumors reached her that Baine had taken refuge there. [[Elerethe Renferal]] and [[Hamuul Runetotem]], two high-ranking Cenarion Circle leaders, were unable to convene their druidic meeting in Moonglade, regarding re-opening trade links between the Alliance and the Horde, due to a wary [[Remulos]], who apparently insisted that they meet initially in Ashenvale due to the potentially explosive nature of their political affairs, but he was willing to allow a second meeting in the Moonglade should their Ashenvale meeting prove successful.\r\nIt was in Moonglade where Malfurion Stormrage was first made aware of the return of the Emerald Nightmare into [[Azeroth]], shortly after the defeat of [[Archimonde]] during the [[war in Draenor]]. This news would prompt the Archdruid to return to [[Val'sharah]] on the [[Broken Isles]].\r\n==Geography==\r\nMoonglade is a hilly forest region dotted with countless mounds, beneath which lay the [[Barrow den|sanctums]] of other druids. The lush forest is untouched by corruption, ancient and strong, and it is surrounded by tall mountains, sheltering it from the outside world. The sacred [[Lake Elune'ara]], named for [[Elune]] herself, can be found in the glade's center. The only land route to the Moonglade runs through the southwestern mountains via [[Timbermaw Hold]]. The entire valley is a haven for druids of both factions, a neutral zone where those in training can learn from the masters and the animals of the forest.\r\n===Instances===\r\nThere are no dungeons of any sort and no battlegrounds in Moonglade.\r\n===Resources===\r\nThough the area is extremely fertile and full of life, there are oddly no useful [[herb]]s here, nor any [[ore]] to speak of. As the creatures inhabiting the zone are all critters (with the exception of the wolves assisting [[Omen]], see ''[[|Wild creatures]]'' below) there is not much for [[skinning|skinners]] to gather either. In contrast, the waters of [[Lake Elune'ara]] are plentiful in [[fish]], particularly [[:Greater Sagefish]].\r\n====[[Flight path]]s from '''Alliance Flight Point'''====\r\n*[[Lor'danel]], [[Darkshore]]\r\n*[[Talonbranch Glade]], [[Felwood]]\r\n*[[Everlook]], [[Winterspring]]\r\n*[[Nordrassil]], [[Mount Hyjal]] \r\n====[[Flight path]]s from '''Horde Flight Point'''====\r\n*[[Irontree Clearing]], [[Felwood]]\r\n*[[Everlook]], [[Winterspring]]\r\n*[[Nordrassil]], [[Mount Hyjal]] \r\n==== [[Flight path]]s from [[Nighthaven]]====\r\n* [[Rut'theran Village]], [[Teldrassil]]\r\n* [[Thunder Bluff]], [[Mulgore]]\r\n==== [[Portal]] at the [[Stormrage Barrow Dens]]====\r\n*[[Emerald Dreamway]], a portal hub within the [[Emerald Dream]]. \r\n==Notable characters==\r\nMoonglade is home to several characters of note. At Nighthaven, [[Dendrite Starblaze]] aids young druids in obtaining the power to attain the bear form, the aquatic form, and to cure poisons. [[Rabine Saturna]] enlists experienced heroes in the battle against the silithid, and at the Shrine of Remulos, [[Keeper Remulos]] attempts to cleanse the taint that has affected the four emerald dragons of the Dream. [[Loganaar]] is the sole [[Druid Trainer]] here. Even [[Malfurion Stormrage]] himself has been known to make an appearance in spirit here.\r\n==Quests==\r\nAfter [[patch 4.0.3a]], Moonglade has no quests of its own that would be classified directly as Moonglade quests. However, some quests send players to Moonglade as a stopgap in larger quest chains (e.g. [[The Keeper's Favor]] and [[Hero's Call: Mount Hyjal!]]/[[Warchief's Command: Mount Hyjal!]]). It is also involved in the [[Lunar Festival]] world event.\r\n===Sentient creatures===\r\n*Dryad\r\n*Keeper of the grove\r\n* [[Green dragon]]s (One, [[Aronus]])\r\n*Humans (one, [[Umber]])\r\n*Jungle trolls (one, [[Zen'Balai]])\r\n*Murlocs\r\n*Night elf\r\n*Tauren\r\n*Wildkin\r\n===Wild creatures===\r\n* [[Deer]]\r\n* [[Frog]]s\r\n* [[Rabbit]]s\r\n===Monsters===\r\n* [[Ancient]]s (One, [[Omen]])\r\n* [[Emerald Nightmare|Nightmare]] [[aberration]]s\r\n* [[Spirit beast]]s\r\n*Undead (Three [[Primal Guardians]])\r\n==Getting there==\r\nAlthough Moonglade is a mostly peaceful and safe zone, it is hard to reach for lower-level characters. To enter it by foot, you first need to go through the entire stretch of [[Felwood]], a level 45-50 zone, starting in [[Ashenvale]].\r\nDruids can learn to [[Teleport: Moonglade|teleport]] themselves to Moonglade at level 14, which makes it very easy for night elf druids to access [[Darnassus]] and [[Darkshore]] when they need to. [[Horde]] druids can teleport there as well, but they are considerably farther away from friendly territory than their Alliance compatriots; even flying straight back to [[Thunder Bluff]] takes seven minutes.\r\nAfter [[To The Dreamgrove]] is completed, [[Dreamwalk]] sends druids to the [[Emerald Dreamway]], where a Moonglade portal is located.\r\nDuring the [[Lunar Festival]], anyone can teleport to Moonglade after completing a quest and can get the flight path for later.\r\nYou can also use a trick to travel there from [[Darkshore]]. If you keep swimming far north from the northern end of its coast, the atmosphere will change to green hills and your zone will be 'Moonglade'. You can enter the land, but not climb the mountains. Enter the water again, but take care that you do not reach 'The Veiled Sea', you must pass through 'The Veiled Sea' however on your way north. Drown yourself, and you will be in Moonglade.\r\nThere are also flight points for those who have managed to get to Moonglade previously, granting easy access in the future.\r\n* [[Flight Point]]: Near the road that runs along the south shore of Lake Elune'Ara.\r\n* [[Flight Point]]: To the northwest of the [[Timbermaw Hold]] entrance.\r\nThere are also neutral flight masters inside Nighthaven who can transport night elf druids to [[Rut'theran Village]] and tauren druids to [[Thunder Bluff]] for free. Non-druids cannot use the services of these flight masters.\r\n==Notes and trivia==\r\n*Moonglade is somewhat more conducive to druidic magic than a large city like [[Darnassus]].\r\n*[[The Warcraft Encyclopedia]] pages refer to the area as the Moonglade of Mount Hyjal.\r\n*Malfurion said that he wanted to move the mad [[Fandral Staghelm]] to the Moonglade as it had places that could hold the sick or corrupted of mind. Yet, Fandral was next seen in Mount Hyjal, from which he was said to be transported to Moonglade.\r\n*Shortly before the [[Cataclysm (event)|Cataclysm]], Remulos planned to host a second meeting between [[Hamuul Runetotem]] and [[Elerethe Renferal]] here.\r\n*Moonglade has four [[flight master]]s ([[Silva Fil'naveth]] and [[Bunthen Plainswind]] in Nighthaven, and [[Sindrayl]] and [[Faustron]] to the south), though the ones in Nighthaven only service [[druid]] characters.\r\n*Although it has a strong lore associated to it, Moonglade is a rather unpopulated zone in World of Warcraft. The reason is a combination of the lack of resources along with the low number of quests (almost none, especially after the Shattering). As a result, the majority of players in the zone are druids using the zone as a second [[hearthstone]] to take a flight path elsewhere.\r\n*On ''[[Warcraft III: Reign of Chaos|Warcraft III]]'' maps, Moonglade was located to the south of Winterspring, east of the Mount Hyjal and northeast of Ashenvale. This seems to have been retconned.\r\n==See also==\r\n*[[Server:Moonglade Europe]]",},
			["Moonglade Isle"] = { content = "'''Moonglade Isle''' is an island in the middle of a lake in the [[Moonglade]]. The [[Horn of Cenarius]] was kept on it guarded by three [[Primal Guardians]] (spirits of ancient [[Keepers]]). The night elf sentinels had to fight their way to the island in order to get the horn so they could wake the sleeping druids.",},
			["Moonglow"] = { content = "==Source==\r\nThis item can be purchased for 15 copper from Lunar Festival Vendor in [[Thunder Bluff]], [[Ironforge]], [[Darnassus]], [[Orgrimmar]], [[Undercity]], [[Moonglade]] and [[Stormwind City]] during the [[Lunar Festival]].",},
			["Moongraze Woods"] = { content = "'''Moongraze Woods''' is the forest surrounding [[Azure Watch]] in the [[Azuremyst Isle]] zone. It is inhabited by roaming [[stag]]s, [[nightstalker]]s and [[lasher]]s.",},
			["Moonguard"] = { content = "#REDIRECT [[Moon Guard]]", redirect = "Moon Guard",},
			["Moonhunters"] = { content = "A faction within the [[night elves]].",},
			["Moonkin"] = { content = "'''Moonkin''' are sapient humanoids native to the [[night elf]] areas in northern [[Kalimdor]]. Sometimes called an \"[[owlbear]]\", nicknamed \"Boomkin\" or jokingly named \"[[OOM]]kin\" by other players, these large bipedal creatures have the size of an upright walking bear, but with bird-like features such as a beak, feathers, and flightless wings. They also drop [[egg]]s of various sorts. They are related to the [[Wildkin]].\r\nAll [[druid]]s must fight a moonkin named [[Lunaclaw]] in order to earn their [[Bear Form]], and if they choose a seventh tier talent in the [[Druid Talents|Balance]] tree druids can assume [[Moonkin Form]] themselves.\r\n==As a mob==\r\n'''Moonkin''' are level 12-13 [[humanoid]]s found in [[Darkshore]].",},
			["Moonkin Form"] = { content = "''Now in two colors: Horned and Night Owl (while supplies last).''\r\n'''Moonkin Form''' enables a Druid to specialize in DPS spellcasting.\r\n==Notes==\r\n* Immune to [[Polymorph]] effects.\r\n* While in this form, you can only cast [[Balance]] spells and [[Remove Curse]].\r\n* When in Moonkin Form you are flagged as a [[humanoid]] and are immune to beast-type magic, like a Druid's [[Hibernate]], or Hunter abilities designed to affect beasts, but you are also immune to polymorph. (It used to be possible to knock a Moonkin out into normal form with [[Hallowed Wand]]s, but this has been fixed.)\r\n* Moonkin is one of only two shapeshift forms in which a druid can use potions and deal weapon damage. (The other is Tree of Life form.) In feral forms, damage dealt is feral, not weapon damage.\r\n* You cannot ride [[mounts]] while in Moonkin Form. You will also need to remove Moonkin Form in order to use a flight path; unlike the other forms, talking to a Flight Master NPC will not force the Druid out of Moonkin Form.*There are a few places were change of appearance can allow you to ride mounts in Moonkin Form,such as places were you get the fel orc costume.Shifting into Moonkin Form will not change your appearance,just give you the bonuses to [[Armor]] and [[Crit]],and it is possible to mount.Leaving such an area will not dismount you but you will gain your moonkin appearance,making you a mounted moonkin.This same trick can be done in [[Wetlands]] with the [[Cursed_Sailor|Cursed Sailors]] \r\n* When in Moonkin Form the [[druid]] dances exactly like when using the [[Gordok Ogre Suit]].\r\n* Melee mana regeneration is through a chance on hit effect called [[Grace of Elune]] and the mana regenerated is 30% of the moonkin's [[Attack Power]] each time it procs. The proc rate seems to be normalized so that fast and slow weapons have the same number of procs per minute (about 15 procs/minute ). Moonkins should have a druid-specific weapon with high attack power hotkeyed so that they switch easily when the time comes to regenerate more mana and the switch back to resume casting.\r\n* It is possible to tank many instances in Moonkin form. However, the talent builds and gear required differ from a DPS role. \r\n* Players have given the moonkin form many nicknames. These are normally short and end with ...nkin or just ....kin, some of these are: Boomkin (a moonkin druid with a high damage output), Oomkin (a moonkin with poor dpm or mana regen), Doomkin (a good PVP moonkin, rarely used), Noob/newbkin (a bad/inexperienced moonkin druid), Panzerkin (a tanking moonkin). Sometimes these nicknames are use to sescribe a particular druid, but most of the time players use them as a general term. Many moonkin druids find these nicknames insulting.\r\n==Tips and tactics==\r\nInvest in as many talents that increase the DPS of your spells, both those that reduce casting time ([[Starlight Wrath]]) and increase damage ([[Moonfury]]). If you are going for a group PvE build, don't invest in talents that require physical contact ([[Brambles]], [[Omen of Clarity]]). However, if you are going for a solo PvE build, then do invest in these talents, and make sure to have [[Barkskin]] active, as you will need it if you're taking damage, even with the 400% armor increase.\r\nWhen out of mana it is extremely useful to equip a Feral Attack Power weapon and melee your target because of the extra mana gain from melee attacks in Moonkin Form.\r\n===Tanking===\r\nMoonkins (\"Panzerkins\") can be a strong alternative to non-tank specs through decent damage mitigation and high DPS (versus [[main tank]] specs). Moonkin tanking is rare for many reasons, but Moonkins have successfully tanked [[Karazhan]], [[Gruul's Lair]] and most 5-man heroics. Gearing is problematic; PvE rewards do not generally support Moonkin tanking, but the [[Arena Rewards]] for druids provide some of the balance necessary. is currently the largest set of information about Moonkin tanking.\r\n===PvE===\r\nMoonkin have three primary abilities that are key to surviving in PvE - Cyclone, Entangling Roots, and Barkskin. Cyclone is obtained at level 70 and allows the druid to temporarily encase a target in a cyclone which makes him immune to all forms of attack (lasts 6 seconds). Entangling Roots snares a target in place for up to 27 seconds and does damage every 3 seconds, however damage to the snared target can remove the effect. Both of these abilities give the Moonkin CC abilities which are essential for those \"whoops, I pulled one too many\" moments. Barkskin reduces all damage taken by 20% and prevents pushback on your spells for 12 seconds. Obviously Barkskin is useful for mitigating damage but it also allows the druid to shift back to caster form and cast some HoTs. Lifebloom and Rejuvenation, along with the bonus healing from Lunar Guidance, increases a Moonkin's survivability considerably. Now one might ask, \"both those HoTs are instant so why should I wait until I cast Barkskin to shift out and use them?\" The answer to that is simple, when you shift out, you lose the 400% bonus to your armor, so you take significantly more damage, Barkskin helps to reduce that loss of armor.\r\nCyclone has diminishing returns in PvE and is therefore not an effective way of CC'ing a particular mob for an extended period of time. After several casts of Cyclone on a particular mob, the mob is immune to the spell.\r\n===PvP===\r\nMoonkin truly shine in PvP. Starfire and Wrath can quickly chip away at an enemy's health while the DoT from Moonfire finishes off anyone who runs away. One thing that should be taken to heart: Moonfire spam is fun and ticks a lot of people off but absolutely destroys your mana supply. Moonfire spam should only be used to finish off a fleeing opponent, or as a last ditch effort to survive. Also, by spamming Moonfire, you never allow its DoT to run its course, because every time you cast Moonfire, its timer resets. If you insist on spamming Moonfire, cast your highest rank first then switch to your second highest. This still deals massive damage but it also allows your DoT to run its course. \r\nInsect Swarm does decent damage per point of mana and its marginal reduction in hit chance isn't too shabby. Entangling Roots, unfortunately, is becoming less useful as time passes because more and more classes are being given ways to escape snare effects. If anything, it still delays a player from reaching you, which usually will give you the time to cast a Starfire/Moonfire combo. Use Starfire from range and Wrath in melee.\r\nMost players will suggest beginning fights in Cat Form. If you are a Night Elf (and patient), simply shadowmeld and wait for your target to come in range then surprise them. Starting from Cat Form has its advantages though. If you are a competent \"stance dancer\" (you should be if you wish to be a Moonkin) you can Pounce and then Rip your target, then switch to Bear Form before they recover from the stun. From Bear Form, melee your target once (possibly twice if you are unlucky) to get enough rage to Bash your target. This gives you enough time to switch to Caster Form and place a Rejuvenation on yourself and switch back into Moonkin. Once back into Moonkin Form, Moonfire your target. At this point the stun should be wearing off. The rest is up to you.",},
			["Moonpetal Lily"] = { content = "==Moonpetal Lily as a quest objective==\r\nThis item is an objective of Iverron's Antidote.\r\n==As an object==\r\nThe '''Moonpetal Lily''' can be found near the lake in western [[Shadowglen]] in [[Teldrassil]].",},
			["Moonrage pack"] = { content = "The simple inhabitants of [[Pyrewood Village]], which is located below the massive [[Shadowfang Keep]], were simple, ordinary people. Due to unknown reasons, most likely due to the odd [[Pyrewood Shackle]]s they wear, the townsfolk turn into rampaging '''Moonrage''' [[Worgen]] at night. The village elders most likely know some information as to the reasons the townsfolk turn into worgen, but yet, the elders remain humanoid at night.\r\nThe fact that the villagers look suprisingly like the [[Son of Arugal|Sons of Arugal]] commonly found in the area may be noted. It can be concluded that when Arugal took control of Shadowfang Keep, his dastardly experiments had a negative effect on the residents of the local village (who were employed at the Keep).",},
			["Moonsoul Crown"] = { content = "==Source==\r\nThis item can be acquired through crafting or another combine-type effect.",},
			["Moonstalker"] = { content = "'''Moonstalkers''' are level 14-15 [[cat]]s found in [[Darkshore]].\r\nA striped, black-colored big cat found only in Darkshore. These beasts are very aggressive, but their beautiful black coloration attracts some [[hunter]]s to tame them. The same black and white striped pelt is shared with [[Blackwind Sabercat]]s, found in the mountains of [[Skettis]].",},
			["Moontouched Owlbeast"] = { content = "'''Moontouched Owlbeast''' is a 57-58 [[Moonkin]] that can be found in [[Winterspring]].\r\n==Drops == \r\n \r\n Quest items dropped by '''Moontouched Owlbeast''' \r\nAlso 1 random [[Uncommon]] item drops\r\nAlso 4 random [[Common]] item drops",},
			["Moonwell"] = { content = "A '''moonwell''' (also spelled '''moon well''') is an upwelling of [[magic]]al waters created by the [[Night elf|night elves]] to maintain and restore their magical powers. They are stone pools filled with silvery glowing water.\r\nLittle is known about the first moon well or how the moon wells proliferated through Azeroth, despite the taboo on overt magical practice among the night elves.\r\n==History and usage==\r\nMoon wells are hallowed repositories of the sacred waters of the [[Well of Eternity (Hyjal)|Well of Eternity]], the pool of energy that gives life to the mystical [[Nordrassil|World Tree]]. When additional water is added, these wells nourish the night elf troops with their life-sustaining waters. Additional moon wells become necessary as the night elf forces grow in number. The first step to establishing a moonwell is to gain the blessings of the local wildlife. It is their goodwill that enables night elves to peacefully coexist, and a moonwell thrives on such energies. After receiving the blessings they are combined into a ritual bundle and imbue the moonwell, followed by water added from a preexisting purified moonwell. Combined with [[Elune]]'s [[moonlight|light]], a moonwell can purify its surroundings for years.\r\nIt is said that [[Illidan Stormrage]] contributed to the creation of the moonwells, likely referring to his creation of the second Well of Eternity.\r\nMoonwells are bound to the magic of nature and the light of Elune and are known as places of healing for both the land around them and those who drink of their waters, possessing extraordinary restorative properties. Magi and other spellcasters can refresh their mana in these pools — a gift from Elune to Azeroth's other defenders. According to [[Tenaron Stormgrip]] in [[Aldrassil]], the water of the moonwell is brought from the Well of Eternity, and [[Sentinels]] revere them as shrines to Elune. The night elven [[druid]]s also take advantage of its properties. They can be commonly found in most [[Temple of Elune (buildings)|Temples of the Moon]], such as in Val'sharah and Darnassus, as well as throughout night elf settlements. In kaldorei society, they are widely revered by the [[druid]]s, [[Sentinels]] and the returned [[Highborne]] alike. [[Mordent Evenshade]] of the [[Shen'dralar]] even commented on how a single moonwell reminded him of the same beauty and purity as the original [[Well of Eternity]].\r\nNight elf priestesses use moonwells to ritualistically cleanse the body of the deceased individual. Moonwells are also used to bless food, offer protection against fire, and bless [[Warden's Arrow]]s. Some moonwells can apparently be used to create the \"[[Liquid Fire of Elune|liquid fire of Elune]]\", a substance that can be poured on animal corpses to cleanse them of [[Scourge]] taint. The waters of the moonwell that rests under the boughs of the [[Oracle Tree]] are said to possess the very essence of Elune's Powers. [[Ashenvale]]'s [[Moonwell of Purity]] is protected by Elune's power.\r\nWater from moonwells can be safely drunk, but the most efficacious use for them is to bathe in the sacred waters, optionally while clad in robes. This act eases feelings of pain, weariness and grief according to [[Astarii Starseeker]].\r\nCorrupted moonwells seem to have the ability to transform people into [[satyr]]s.\r\nFollowing the [[Argus Campaign]] and the destruction of [[Silithus]], night elf priestesses and druids built moonwells there to help restore the devastated land, but the extent of their effectiveness in healing the wound remain unclear.\r\n==In-game uses of a Moonwell==\r\nIn ''World of Warcraft'', moonwells are typically only cosmetic or quest and material-creation (like [[mooncloth]] and [[primal mooncloth]]) related, located mostly in night elf areas. Some newer players used to sometimes be seen standing in a moonwell after combat, with the uninformed belief that it is healing them faster (As was similar in Warcraft 3).\r\n*[[Tailoring|Tailors]] can purify [[Felcloth]] into [[Mooncloth]] and create [[Primal Mooncloth]] only when standing at or in a moonwell.\r\n*Various quests such as [[As Water Cascades]] and [[The Sacred Flame (quest)]] involves tapping water from moonwells.\r\n===Kalimdor===\r\n*[[Ashenvale]]: Various places:\r\n**[[Raynewood Retreat]]\r\n**[[Moonwell (Ashenvale)|Shaeldryn's moonwell]], east of [[Iris Lake]]\r\n**[[Moonwell of Purity]]\r\n**[[Moonwell of Cleansing]]\r\n*[[Azshara]]: [[Talrendis Point]]\r\n**Southern moonwell, east of [[Mystral Lake]]\r\n*[[Darkshore]]: Various places, [[Ruins of Auberdine]], [[Lor'danel]], [[Blackfathom Deeps]] (lore)\r\n*[[Desolace]]: [[Nijel's Point]]\r\n*[[Felwood]]: Various places (The first two are corrupted, but can still be used to purify [[Felcloth]] into [[Mooncloth]]):\r\n**[[Jaedenar]]\r\n**[[Ruins of Constellas]]\r\n**[[Whisperwind Grove]] (uncorrupted)\r\n*[[Feralas]]: [[Feathermoon Stronghold]], [[Dire Maul]]\r\n*[[Moonglade]]: [[Nighthaven]]\r\n*[[Mount Hyjal]]: [[Grove of Aessina]]\r\n*[[Silithus]]: [[Cenarion Hold]]\r\n*[[Stonetalon Mountains]]: [[Stonetalon Peak]]\r\n*[[Teldrassil]]: Various settlements, including [[Dolanaar]]\r\n**[[Darnassus]]: [[Temple of the Moon]] (cannot be used in tailoring)\r\n*[[Thousand Needles]]: [[Thalanaar]]\r\n*[[Tanaris]]: [[Caverns of Time]] (near the entrance for the [[Battle of Mount Hyjal]], can be used to create Primal Mooncloth as of Feb 14, 2008). Addendum: Currently not working as of Oct 11, 2018 for Primal Mooncloth.\r\n===Eastern Kingdoms===\r\n*[[Duskwood]]: In the [[Twilight Grove]]\r\n*[[Ghostlands]]: On [[Shalandis Isle]]\r\n*[[Wetlands]]: [[Greenwarden's Grove]]\r\n*[[Stormwind City]]: In the [[Park]]. Destroyed by [[Deathwing]] along with the rest of the Park.\r\n===Outland===\r\n*[[Blade's Edge Mountains]]: [[Evergrove]], [[Sylvanaar]]\r\n*[[Terokkar Forest]]: [[Cenarion Thicket]]\r\n*[[Zangarmarsh]]: [[Cenarion Refuge]]\r\n===Northrend===\r\n*[[Dragonblight]]: [[Stars' Rest]]\r\n===Firelands===\r\n*[[Molten Front]]: [[Malfurion's Breach]] (phased, based on character completion of quests)\r\n===Draenor===\r\nNone of the moonwells in Draenor can be used in tailoring.\r\n*: [[Starfall Outpost]]\r\n*[[Ashran]]: [[Stormshield]], night elf camp behind the auction house\r\n===Broken Isles===\r\nNone of the moonwells on the Broken Isles can be used in tailoring.\r\n*[[Val'sharah]]: [[Lightsong]], [[Dreamgrove]], road to the Dreamgrove, [[Wildwood]]\r\n*[[Suramar]]: [[Irongrove Retreat]] (after completing [[Eminent Grow-main]])\r\n*[[Broken Shore]]: [[Nether Disruptor]]\r\n====Moonglade====\r\nEnchanted pools throughout the [[Moonglade]] give the [[Night elf|night elves]] their spiritual power and feed the [[Nordrassil]], [[World Tree]] that stands in [[Hyjal Summit]]. The shimmering waters within give off a blue light, causing the moon wells to glow slightly in the night. They are scattered throughout the forest, often near giant standing stones covered in ancient runes.\r\n====Theramore====\r\nThe [[High elf|high elves]] of [[Theramore Isle]], having left mostly before the destruction of [[Dalaran]] and [[Quel'Thalas (kingdom)|Quel'Thalas]], have formed a significant community in the city. They spend a great deal of time hunting the few [[undead]] forces in [[Kalimdor]]. Their exposure to the night elves has caused them to develop a great interest in moon wells, which they seek to find an alternative solution to their addiction. Even the presence of a hidden moon well 50 feet away is enough to replenish their mystical energies and makes meditation unnecessary.\r\nTheramore's high elves also have another interest in the continent. They have discussed privately the creation of their own realm on Kalimdor. The northern forests, full of moon wells and lush greenery are most attractive, but their control by the night elves is overly frustrating. High elven expeditions, claiming to be tracking undead, often search for suitable sites.\r\n==Notes and trivia==\r\n*A moonwell features as an attraction in the [[Blizzard World]] in-universe map in ''[[Overwatch franchise|Overwatch]]'', but is not seen in the in-game map itself.\r\n*Moonwells appear as the Alliance s in the [[Alterac Valley|Alterac Pass]] battleground in ''[[Heroes of the Storm]]''.\r\n*The moonwell in [[Twilight Grove]] is used to restore the [[Torch of Holy Flame]] from [[unholy]] corruption in the short story ''[[Terror by Torchlight]]''.\r\n* is a beverage in the ''[[StarCraft]]'' universe. The drink itself features an image of a moonwell as it appeared in ''Warcraft III''.\r\n==See also==\r\n*[[Sunwell]]",},
			["Moonwell (Ashenvale)"] = { content = "There are three '''Moonwells''' in [[Ashenvale]]. [[Shael'dryn]]'s moonwell is located in the northern part, east of [[Iris Lake]] and west of [[Raynewood Retreat]]. The southern moonwell is located west of [[Silverwing Outpost]] and southeast of [[Greenpaw Village]]. The former is oft visited by [[Alliance]] adventurers who are following the [[Quest:Raene's Cleansing|Raene's Cleansing]] quest chain, and the latter is sometimes visited by [[Horde]] [[shaman]]s doing their [[Quest:Call of Water|Call of Water]] quest chain. The third moonwell is located at Raynewood Retreat .",},
			["Moonwing Den"] = { content = "'''Moonwing Den''' is a series of small [[moonkin]] camps on [[Silvermyst Isle]]. The owlbeasts are very aggressive and caution should be excercised when exploring the area.",},
			["Moon Guard"] = { content = "The '''Moon Guard''' was a [[night elf]] organization. It consisted of sorcerers and, during the [[War of the Ancients]], was led by senior member [[Latosius]]. They were considered by the [[Highborne]] to be of a lower class, as the Moon Guard members were not the elites. Nevertheless, they believed that lord counsellor Xavius was the influence behind the Highborne's envy and not Queen Azshara — whom they worshipped. Before the outbreak of the ancient war, the Moon Guard served Queen [[Azshara]], but when the demons of the [[Burning Legion]] came, it joined the Kaldorei Resistance along with the noble class against the Highborne. The Kaldorei Resistance, including the Moon Guard, was commanded by Lord Ravencrest. After the assassination of Lord Ravencrest, Lord [[Stareye]] took up the leadership of the resistance until he was killed by the [[Doomguard]]. The Kaldorei Resistance, however, regrouped under the famous [[Jarod Shadowsong]] and became victorious against the demons.\r\n[[Illidan Stormrage]] was once the personal sorcerer of Ravencrest, and later led the sorcerers of the Moon Guard when they fought against the [[Burning Legion]].",},
			["Moon Horror Den"] = { content = "'''Moon Horror Den''' is a small cave habited by [[Raging Owlbeast]] Note: they are most likely not there because of players doing the [[wild guardians]] quest. It is situated quite close to [[Everlook]], just a short walk to the northeast from the city gates. Despite its apparent closeness to the [[Winterfall Village]] however, the mountain itself blocks a direct path and a long ride around is needed to head further south from the cave.",},
			["Moon Priestess Amara"] = { content = "'''Moon Priestess Amara''' is a level 25 [[quest giver]] located on the road west of [[Dolanaar]] in the [[night elf]] starting zone, [[Teldrassil]].\r\nShe starts the quest The Road to Darnassus.\r\nSee [[List of Teldrassil NPCs]].",},
			["Moon well"] = { content = "#REDIRECT [[Moonwell]]", redirect = "Moonwell",},
			["Moon wells"] = { content = "#REDIRECT [[Moonwell]]", redirect = "Moonwell",},
			["Moorabi"] = { content = "'''Moorabi''' is a boss of [[Gundrak]], an instance in [[Zul'Drak]].\r\n===Encounter in [[Gun'Drak]]===\r\nUpon aggroing:\r\n* \"We fought back the Scourge. What chance you be thinking you got?\"\r\nWhen using Quake:\r\n* \"The ground will swallow you up!\"\r\nWhen transforming:\r\n* \"Get ready for something much bigger!\"\r\nUpon slaying a player:\r\n* \"I crush you, cockroaches!\"\r\n* \"Who gonna stop me; you?\r\n* \"Not so tough now.\"\r\nUpon death:\r\n* \"If our gods can die, then so can we.\"",},
			["Moose"] = { content = "Moose are animals that are much larger relatives of [[elk]]. The mighty northern alpine moose is one of the primary prey of wolves and other predators. Orcs prefer the challenge of a moose or elk over smaller deer.",},
			["Mor'Ladim"] = { content = "'''Mor'Ladim''' is a level 30 elite armored [[skeleton]] who mindlessly wanders the grounds of [[Raven Hill Cemetery]] in [[Duskwood]].\r\n==Background==\r\nMor'Ladim was formerly [[Morgan Ladimore]], bearer of the sword [[Archeus]], whose lone grave rests on the hillside north of the cemetery. In life, Ladimore committed a sin for which he felt great sorrow, and now, in death, he cannot rest until someone can relieve him of his constant pain. His daughter [[Watcher Ladimore|Sarah Ladimore]] is now a member of the [[Night Watch]] in [[Darkshire]].\r\n[[Commander Althea Ebonlocke]] wants Mor'Ladim killed.\r\n==Objective of==\r\n*Drops Mor'Ladim's Skull for the quest Mor'Ladim.\r\n==Notes==\r\nPrior to patch 2.3 Mor'Ladim was elite and was famous for catching level 20-something questers off-guard and sending them to the closest spirit healer. He is also still famous for his incredibly large aggro radius for the zone level.\r\nAs of patch 2.4.3 at least, Mor'Ladim has regained his elite status; and it's still present in patch 2.4.3.",},
			["Mor'shan Base Camp"] = { content = "One of the more sizable Horde villages in the northern [[Barrens]], Mor'shan Base Camp is located just south of the [[Ashenvale]]-Barrens border and is home to the families of many Orcish warriors who are currently fighting for the Warsong to the north. It is also the location of the Horde entrance to the [[Warsong Gulch]] Battleground.\r\n==Merchants==\r\nKelm Hargunth \r\nHecht Copperpinch",},
			["Mor'shan Rampart"] = { content = "'''The Mor'shan Rampart''' lies at the northern terminus of the [[Gold Road]] in [[the Barrens]]. This makeshift defensive post was built to withstand the push of [[Alliance]] forces into the [[Barrens]] from [[Ashenvale]] to the north. There is, however, a damaged portion unguarded by the Horde to the east of the main post. It is mostly abandoned, but still serves as a makeshift launching point for raids on the [[Night Elf]] town of [[Astranaar]].",},
			["Mor'zul's Instructions"] = { content = "==Source==\r\nThis item is provided for Dreadsteed of Xoroth.",},
			["Mor'zul Bloodbringer"] = { content = "'''Mor'zul Bloodbringer''' is a level 61 [[quest giver]] located just west of the [[Altar of Storms]] in the [[contested]] territory of [[Burning Steppes]].\r\nHe starts the following quests:\r\n* Rage of Blood\r\n* Wildeyes\r\n* Doomsday Candle\r\n* Bell of Dethmoora\r\n* Wheel of the Black March\r\n* Dreadsteed of Xoroth (Dungeon)\r\nSee [[List of Burning Steppes NPCs]].",},
			["Moragg"] = { content = "'''Moragg''' is a [[floating eye]] boss located in the [[Violet Hold]].\r\n==Tactics==",},
			["Morass Road"] = { content = "The '''Morass Road''' was a path through the [[Black Morass]] before and during the [[First War]]. The [[human]]s of [[Stormwind (kingdom)|Stormwind]] usually kept to the road, not entering the swamp itself.",},
			["Morbent's Bane"] = { content = "'''Morbent's Bane''' is a [[off-hand]] item. [[Sven Yorgen]] sends adventurers to forge a weapon capable of defeating [[Morbent Fel]]. [[Lightforge Ingot]]s salvaged from the sunken [[high elf|elven]] [[Destroyer|destroyer]], the ''[[Flying Osprey]]'', are used in its creation.\r\nThe [[Torch of Holy Flame]] is the quest reward version of this item.\r\n==Source==\r\nThis item is used for the following quests:\r\n* [[Morbent Fel (quest)]]\r\n* [[Armed and Ready]]",},
			["Morbent Fel"] = { content = "'''Morbent Fel''' is a level 32 [[elite]] [[named]] [[necromancer]] who rules over the [[undead]] of [[Duskwood]] from his surprisingly homely house atop the [[Forlorn Rowe]] in [[Raven Hill Cemetery]]. He is guarded by his undead minions as well as a magical barrier that dampens attacks on his person.\r\nIn order to defeat him, one must first take off his shield using [[Morbent's Bane]], an offhand item rewarded as a part of his quest chain. If you do not remove his ability, it appears as though he has over 10000 armor to all resistance so do not try it without the bane, unless you're really higher level than him.\r\nFel does not seem affiliated with the [[Lich King]]. His consorting with the [[Black Riders]] shows that he is not directly allied to the [[Scourge]], unless the Black Riders are somehow affiliated with it.\r\n==Attacks and Abilities==\r\n*Unholy Shield: Increases the caster's armor and resistance to spells for 10 min. 10 second cooldown.\r\n*Presence of Death: Utterly terrifies all enemies in a selected area, rendering them unable to move or attack for 10 sec. 1 second cast, 10 second cooldown.\r\n*Touch of Death: Drains 65 to 75 health from an enemy, healing the caster for up to half that amount. 3 second cast.\r\n==Notes==\r\n*Prior to [[Patch 1.6 (Release Notes)|Patch 1.6]], Morbent Fel was a level 35 elite.\r\n*When fighting Fel, be sure to equip Morbent's bane ''before'' beginning the fight, so you can use it immediately.\r\n*[[Dextren ward]], a boss in the [[Stockade]] was caught selling bodies to Morbent Fel from [[Raven Hill Cemetery]]\r\n==Quests==\r\n*Morbent Fel",},
			["Morbent Fel (quest)"] = { content = "This quest concludes the quest chain.\r\n==Objectives==\r\nUse [[Morbent's Bane]] on [[Morbent Fel]], kill Morbent Fel,\r\nthen return Morbent's Bane to [[Sven Yorgen|Sven]] at his camp.\r\n* Morbent's Bane - provided\r\n==Quest Text==\r\n[[Morbent Fel]] hides in his lair, the house perched atop the hill to the\r\neast overlooking the [[Raven Hill]] cemetery. His time in this land is drawing\r\nto an end...\r\nUse Morbent's Bane against him. It will render his protective magics powerless.\r\nSlay him. Slay him, and save us from his wickedness. Be the instrument of\r\nmy revenge, and a hero of Duskwood!\r\n==Progress==\r\nIs Morbent Fel defeated?!\r\n==Completion==\r\nMorbent Fel has been defeated. The dark riders are still at large, but a\r\nsmall piece of that which I had hoped beyond hope has come to pass.\r\nYou have done the impossible, and your deeds will forever live in the\r\nlegends of Duskwood.\r\nGo, <name>. And perhaps, one day, fate may bring you back to me...\r\n==Rewards==\r\n* +500 [[Stormwind]] reputation\r\n* 3850 [[XP]]\r\n==Notes==\r\nThe rewards from this quest include a piece of head armor, one of the lowest\r\nlevel quests to provide such a reward.\r\n[[Morbent Fel]] is in the top floor of the house just east of Sven. He has\r\nthree guards in the room with him. A group is highly recommended for this\r\nquest.\r\nWhile it is possible to cause damage to Morbent Fel without first using\r\n[[Morbent's Bane]], it is exteremely difficult. As Morbent's Bane is an\r\noffhanded item, attempting to use it will put it in your offhand slot first.\r\nBe prepared and have it equipped before you attempt to take him down. \r\nIt has been reported that some rogues, level 30+ have been able to solo this\r\nby sapping Morbent Fel then taking out the guards and [[Vanish]]ing.",},
			["Mordant Grimsby"] = { content = "'''Mordant Grimsby''' is a level 42 [[quest giver]] located at [[Swamplight Manor]] deep in the [[the Quagmire]] in [[Dustwallow Marsh]].\r\nHe starts the following quests:\r\n* What's Haunting Witch Hill?\r\n* The Witch's Bane\r\n* Cleansing Witch Hill\r\nSee [[List of Dustwallow Marsh NPCs]].",},
			["More Components of Importance"] = { content = "During the quest chain to upgrade the [[Dungeon Set 1]] Helm and Chestpiece to [[Dungeon Set 2]], adventurers will have to complete a quest called '''More Components of Importance'''. This quest could be one of four quests:\r\n*[[Quest:More Components of Importance (Tyr's Hand)|Tyr's Hand]] - Retrieve a Brilliant Sword of Zealotry from Tyr's Hand and return it to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.\r\n**Follow up Quest:[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Stratholme)|The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Stratholme)]].\r\n*[[Quest:More Components of Importance (Purgation Isle)|Purgation Isle]] - Obtain Soul Ashes of the Banished from Purgation Isle and return them to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.\r\n**Follow up Quest:[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Scholomance)|The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Scholomance)]].\r\n*[[Quest:More Components of Importance (Hive'Regal)|Hive'Regal]] - Acquire Druidical Remains from Hive'Regal and return them to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain. \r\n**Follow up Quest:[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Lower Blackrock Spire)|The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Lower Blackrock Spire)]].\r\n*[[Quest:More Components of Importance (Frostwhisper Gorge)|Frostwhisper Gorge]] - Acquire a Starbreeze Village Relic from Frostwhisper Gorge and return it to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.\r\n**Follow up Quest:[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Dire Maul)|The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Dire Maul)]].\r\nThe quest you receive is based on which '''Components of Importance''' quest you completed earlier.\r\n*If you completed the Hive'Regal quest for '''Components of Importance''', you will get the Tyr's Hand quest for '''More Components of Importance'''.\r\n*If you completed the Purgation Isle quest for '''Components of Importance''', you will get the Hive'Regal quest for '''More Components of Importance'''.\r\n*If you completed the Frostwhisper Gorge quest for '''Components of Importance''', you will get the Purgation Isle quest for '''More Components of Importance'''.\r\n*If you completed the Tyr's Hand quest for '''Components of Importance''', you will get the Frostwhisper Gorge quest for '''More Components of Importance'''.\r\n==Addendum==\r\nThe matrix for which first component quest and the successor quest is at least '''incorrect''' for my experience, as of patch 1.12.1. My first '''Components of Importance''' was for Purgation Isle, but my second was for Tyr's Hand.\r\nNote 2: Here too, I've got my first '''Components of Importance''' as Hive'Regal, but my second was Frostwhisper Gorge.\r\nNote 3: As of patch 2.0.12, my first '''Components of Importance''' was for Purgation Isle, but my second was also for Tyr's Hand.\r\nNote 4: As of patch 2.4, my first '''Components of Importance''' was for Purgation Isle, and my second was for Hive'Regal. (Seems to be a random pairing each time)",},
			["More Components of Importance (Frostwhisper Gorge)"] = { content = "==Task==\r\n'''Acquire a [[Starbreeze Village Relic]] and return it to [[Bodley]] inside [[Blackrock Mountain]].'''\r\n''<Class>, listen closely. Now that we have the brazier, and the means to light it, we still need another component to suffuse it with; something that will provide a focus strong enough to entice the spirit of my deceased, former comrade.''\r\n''Isalien, our priestess, grew up in Winterspring at Starbreeze Village. I need you to gather a Starbreeze Village Relic from the Frostmaul giants of Frostwhisper Gorge in southern Winterspring, who are known for raiding to the north from time to time.''\r\n==Reward==\r\n3x [[Bloodkelp Elixir of Dodging]] or 3x [[Bloodkelp Elixir of Resistance]]\r\n==Quest Chain==\r\n*[[Quest:Bodley's Unfortunate Fate|Bodley's Unfortunate Fate]]: [[Quest:Bodley's Unfortunate Fate (Alliance)|Alliance]]/[[Quest:Bodley's Unfortunate Fate (Horde)|Horde]]\r\n**[[Quest:Three Kings of Flame|Three Kings of Flame]]\r\n**[[Quest:Components of Importance|Components of Importance]]: [[Quest:Components of Importance (Tyr's Hand)|Tyr's Hand]]/[[Quest:Components of Importance (Purgation Isle)|Purgation Isle]]/[[Quest:Components of Importance (Hive'Regal)|Hive'Regal]]/[[Quest:Components of Importance (Frostwhisper Gorge)|Frostwhisper Gorge]]\r\n**[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet|The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet]]: [[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Stratholme)|Stratholme]]/[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Scholomance)|Scholomance]]/[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Lower Blackrock Spire)|Lower Blackrock Spire]]/[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Dire Maul)|Dire Maul]]\r\n**[[Quest:I See Alcaz Island In Your Future...|I See Alcaz Island In Your Future...]]\r\n**[[Quest:More Components of Importance|More Components of Importance]]: [[Quest:More Components of Importance (Tyr's Hand)|Tyr's Hand]]/[[Quest:More Components of Importance (Purgation Isle)|Purgation Isle]]/[[Quest:More Components of Importance (Hive'Regal)|Hive'Regal]]/'''Frostwhisper Gorge'''\r\n**[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet|The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet]]: [[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Stratholme)|Stratholme]]/[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Scholomance)|Scholomance]]/[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Lower Blackrock Spire)|Lower Blackrock Spire]]/[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Dire Maul)|Dire Maul]]\r\n**[[Quest:Final Preparations|Final Preparations]]\r\n**[[Quest:Mea Culpa, Lord Valthalak|Mea Culpa, Lord Valthalak]]\r\n***[[Quest:Return to Bodley|Return to Bodley]]\r\n***[[Quest:Back to the Beginning|Back to the Beginning]]: [[Quest:Back to the Beginning (Alliance)|Alliance]]/[[Quest:Back to the Beginning (Horde)|Horde]]\r\n***[[Quest:Saving the Best for Last|Saving the Best for Last]]: [[Quest:Saving the Best for Last (Alliance)|Alliance]]/[[Quest:Saving the Best for Last (Horde)|Horde]]\r\n==Notes==\r\n*This is the sixth step in the quest chain to upgrade your [[Dungeon Set 1]] Helm and Chestpiece into [[Dungeon Set 2]].\r\n*The relic is dropped dropped by the [[Frostmaul]] [[giant]]s in southern [[Winterspring]].\r\n*The next step in the quest chain is [[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Dire Maul)|The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Dire Maul)]].\r\n----\r\nGo to [[Quests]]",},
			["More Components of Importance (Hive'Regal)"] = { content = "==Task==\r\n'''Acquire [[Druidical Remains]] and return them to [[Bodley]] inside [[Blackrock Mountain]].'''\r\n''<Class>, listen closely. Now that we have the brazier, and the means to light it, we still need another component to suffuse it with; something that will provide a focus strong enough to entice the spirit of my deceased, former comrade.''\r\n''Mor Grayhoof, our most prominent druid, had many close friends amongst the [[Cenarion Circle]], some of which have fallen to the silithid. I need you to retrieve some Druidical Remains from the silithid that inhabit the environs of [[Hive'Regal]] in southeastern Silithus.''\r\n==Reward==\r\n3x [[Bloodkelp Elixir of Dodging]] or 3x [[Bloodkelp Elixir of Resistance]]\r\n==Quest Chain==\r\n*[[Quest:Bodley's Unfortunate Fate|Bodley's Unfortunate Fate]]: [[Quest:Bodley's Unfortunate Fate (Alliance)|Alliance]]/[[Quest:Bodley's Unfortunate Fate (Horde)|Horde]]\r\n**[[Quest:Three Kings of Flame|Three Kings of Flame]]\r\n**[[Quest:Components of Importance|Components of Importance]]: [[Quest:Components of Importance (Tyr's Hand)|Tyr's Hand]]/[[Quest:Components of Importance (Purgation Isle)|Purgation Isle]]/[[Quest:Components of Importance (Hive'Regal)|Hive'Regal]]/[[Quest:Components of Importance (Frostwhisper Gorge)|Frostwhisper Gorge]]\r\n**[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet|The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet]]: [[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Stratholme)|Stratholme]]/[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Scholomance)|Scholomance]]/[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Lower Blackrock Spire)|Lower Blackrock Spire]]/[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Dire Maul)|Dire Maul]]\r\n**[[Quest:I See Alcaz Island In Your Future...|I See Alcaz Island In Your Future...]]\r\n**[[Quest:More Components of Importance|More Components of Importance]]: [[Quest:More Components of Importance (Tyr's Hand)|Tyr's Hand]]/[[Quest:More Components of Importance (Purgation Isle)|Purgation Isle]]/'''Hive'Regal'''/[[Quest:More Components of Importance (Frostwhisper Gorge)|Frostwhisper Gorge]]\r\n**[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet|The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet]]: [[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Stratholme)|Stratholme]]/[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Scholomance)|Scholomance]]/[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Lower Blackrock Spire)|Lower Blackrock Spire]]/[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Dire Maul)|Dire Maul]]\r\n**[[Quest:Final Preparations|Final Preparations]]\r\n**[[Quest:Mea Culpa, Lord Valthalak|Mea Culpa, Lord Valthalak]]\r\n***[[Quest:Return to Bodley|Return to Bodley]]\r\n***[[Quest:Back to the Beginning|Back to the Beginning]]: [[Quest:Back to the Beginning (Alliance)|Alliance]]/[[Quest:Back to the Beginning (Horde)|Horde]]\r\n***[[Quest:Saving the Best for Last|Saving the Best for Last]]: [[Quest:Saving the Best for Last (Alliance)|Alliance]]/[[Quest:Saving the Best for Last (Horde)|Horde]]\r\n==Notes==\r\n*This is the sixth step in the quest chain to upgrade your [[Dungeon Set 1]] Helm and Chestpiece into [[Dungeon Set 2]].\r\n*[[Hive'Regal]] can be found in southeast [[Silithus]].\r\n*The remains are dropped by the [[Silithid]] in Hive'Regal.\r\n*The next step in the quest chain is [[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Lower Blackrock Spire)|The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Lower Blackrock Spire)]].\r\n----\r\nGo to [[Quests]]",},
			["More Components of Importance (Purgation Isle)"] = { content = "= Task =\r\n'''Obtain [[Soul Ashes of the Banished]] and return them to [[Bodley]] inside [[Blackrock Mountain]].'''\r\n''<Class>, listen closely. Now that we have the brazier, and the means to light it, we still need another component to suffuse it with; something that will provide a focus strong enough to entice the spirit of my deceased, former comrade.''\r\n''An ogre necromancer that traveled with us, Kormok, delighted in summoning forth the souls of the banished dead of Purgation Isle, off the south coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Go there and retrieve some Soul Ashes of the Banished from their remains.''\r\n= Reward =\r\n3x [[Bloodkelp Elixir of Dodging]] or 3x [[Bloodkelp Elixir of Resistance]]\r\n= Quest Chain =\r\n*[[Quest:Bodley's Unfortunate Fate|Bodley's Unfortunate Fate]]: [[Quest:Bodley's Unfortunate Fate (Alliance)|Alliance]]/[[Quest:Bodley's Unfortunate Fate (Horde)|Horde]]\r\n**[[Quest:Three Kings of Flame|Three Kings of Flame]]\r\n**[[Quest:Components of Importance|Components of Importance]]: [[Quest:Components of Importance (Tyr's Hand)|Tyr's Hand]]/[[Quest:Components of Importance (Purgation Isle)|Purgation Isle]]/[[Quest:Components of Importance (Hive'Regal)|Hive'Regal]]/[[Quest:Components of Importance (Frostwhisper Gorge)|Frostwhisper Gorge]]\r\n**[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet|The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet]]: [[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Stratholme)|Stratholme]]/[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Scholomance)|Scholomance]]/[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Lower Blackrock Spire)|Lower Blackrock Spire]]/[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Dire Maul)|Dire Maul]]\r\n**[[Quest:I See Alcaz Island In Your Future...|I See Alcaz Island In Your Future...]]\r\n**[[Quest:More Components of Importance|More Components of Importance]]: [[Quest:More Components of Importance (Tyr's Hand)|Tyr's Hand]]/'''Purgation Isle'''/[[Quest:More Components of Importance (Hive'Regal)|Hive'Regal]]/[[Quest:More Components of Importance (Frostwhisper Gorge)|Frostwhisper Gorge]]\r\n**[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet|The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet]]: [[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Stratholme)|Stratholme]]/[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Scholomance)|Scholomance]]/[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Lower Blackrock Spire)|Lower Blackrock Spire]]/[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Dire Maul)|Dire Maul]]\r\n**[[Quest:Final Preparations|Final Preparations]]\r\n**[[Quest:Mea Culpa, Lord Valthalak|Mea Culpa, Lord Valthalak]]\r\n***[[Quest:Return to Bodley|Return to Bodley]]\r\n***[[Quest:Back to the Beginning|Back to the Beginning]]: [[Quest:Back to the Beginning (Alliance)|Alliance]]/[[Quest:Back to the Beginning (Horde)|Horde]]\r\n***[[Quest:Saving the Best for Last|Saving the Best for Last]]: [[Quest:Saving the Best for Last (Alliance)|Alliance]]/[[Quest:Saving the Best for Last (Horde)|Horde]]\r\n= Notes = \r\n*This is the sixth step in the quest chain to upgrade your [[Dungeon Set 1]] Helm and Chestpiece into [[Dungeon Set 2]].\r\n*Purgation Isle is off the coast of the [[Hillsbrad Foothills]]. It is southwest from the [[Azurelode Mine]].\r\n*The ashes are dropped by the [[Undead]] on the isle such as Condemned Acolytes, Condemned Clerics, and Cursed Paladins.\r\n*The next step in the quest chain is [[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Scholomance)|The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Scholomance)]].\r\n----\r\nGo to [[Quests]]",},
			["More Components of Importance (Tyr's Hand)"] = { content = "==Task==\r\n'''Retrieve a [[Brilliant Sword of Zealotry]] and return it to [[Bodley]] inside [[Blackrock Mountain]].'''\r\n''<class>, listen closely. Now that we have the brazier, and the means to light it, we still need another component to suffuse it with; something that will provide a focus strong enough to summon the remains of my deceased, former comrades.''\r\n''The siblings, Jarien and Sothos, were believers in the way of the Scarlet Crusade. They aspired to knighthood within that vile organization. Go to Tyr's Hand in Eastern Plaguelands and retrieve a Brilliant Sword of Zealotry from the praetorians there.''\r\n==Reward==\r\n3x [[Bloodkelp Elixir of Dodging]] or 3x [[Bloodkelp Elixir of Resistance]]\r\n==Quest Chain==\r\n*[[Quest:Bodley's Unfortunate Fate|Bodley's Unfortunate Fate]]: [[Quest:Bodley's Unfortunate Fate (Alliance)|Alliance]]/[[Quest:Bodley's Unfortunate Fate (Horde)|Horde]]\r\n**[[Quest:Three Kings of Flame|Three Kings of Flame]]\r\n**[[Quest:Components of Importance|Components of Importance]]: [[Quest:Components of Importance (Tyr's Hand)|Tyr's Hand]]/[[Quest:Components of Importance (Purgation Isle)|Purgation Isle]]/[[Quest:Components of Importance (Hive'Regal)|Hive'Regal]]/[[Quest:Components of Importance (Frostwhisper Gorge)|Frostwhisper Gorge]]\r\n**[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet|The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet]]: [[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Stratholme)|Stratholme]]/[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Scholomance)|Scholomance]]/[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Lower Blackrock Spire)|Lower Blackrock Spire]]/[[Quest:The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Dire Maul)|Dire Maul]]\r\n**[[Quest:I See Alcaz Island In Your Future...|I See Alcaz Island In Your Future...]]\r\n**[[Quest:More Components of Importance|More Components of Importance]]: '''Tyr's Hand'''/[[Quest:More Components of Importance (Purgation Isle)|Purgation Isle]]/[[Quest:More Components of Importance (Hive'Regal)|Hive'Regal]]/[[Quest:More Components of Importance (Frostwhisper Gorge)|Frostwhisper Gorge]]\r\n**[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet|The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet]]: [[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Stratholme)|Stratholme]]/[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Scholomance)|Scholomance]]/[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Lower Blackrock Spire)|Lower Blackrock Spire]]/[[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Dire Maul)|Dire Maul]]\r\n**[[Quest:Final Preparations|Final Preparations]]\r\n**[[Quest:Mea Culpa, Lord Valthalak|Mea Culpa, Lord Valthalak]]\r\n***[[Quest:Return to Bodley|Return to Bodley]]\r\n***[[Quest:Back to the Beginning|Back to the Beginning]]: [[Quest:Back to the Beginning (Alliance)|Alliance]]/[[Quest:Back to the Beginning (Horde)|Horde]]\r\n***[[Quest:Saving the Best for Last|Saving the Best for Last]]: [[Quest:Saving the Best for Last (Alliance)|Alliance]]/[[Quest:Saving the Best for Last (Horde)|Horde]]\r\n==Notes==\r\n*This is the sixth step in the quest chain to upgrade your [[Dungeon Set 1]] Helm and Chestpiece into [[Dungeon Set 2]].\r\n*The sword is dropped by Scarlet Praetorians at [[Tyr's Hand]] in southeast [[Eastern Plaguelands]]. They are level 51-57 elites.\r\n*The next step in the quest chain is [[Quest:The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Stratholme)|The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet (Stratholme)]]\r\n----\r\nGo to [[Quests]]",},
			["More Crystal Fragments"] = { content = "==Objectives==\r\nCollect 10 Oshu'gun Crystal Fragments and return them to [[Gezhe]] at Aeris Landing in [[Nagrand]].\r\nCollect:\r\n* 10 [[Oshu'gun Crystal Fragment]]\r\n==Details==\r\nGehze is located on the southern side of Aeris Landing, near the road. The quest items can be looted directly off the ground in the areas surrounding the Oshu'Gun Diamond or the nearby satellite diamonds just south of Aeris Landing, or as drops from the Ethereals surrounding those areas.\r\nThis quest is repeatable, until you are with [[The Consortium]]. The fragments can be traded to other players.\r\n==Description==\r\n''You've got more crystal fragments? Make sure you're not taking any that are still attached to the mountain; we wouldn't want to stir up trouble with the naaru.''\r\n==Completion==\r\nKeep the crystal fragments coming, ''<name>''. We cannot let these thieves take our property.\r\nEven if it's not ours just quite yet. A technicality, of course.\r\n==Quest Progression==\r\n# Stealing from Thieves\r\n# More Crystal Fragments [[RRQ]]",},
			["More Heads Full of Ivory"] = { content = "==Objectives==\r\nI still have a need for more pairs of ivory tusks from the wild elekk that roam this land. Unfortunately, my budget will no longer handle your cut of the profits. If you continue to provide me what I need, however, you will be ingratiating yourself with the Consortium. \r\n* Pair of Ivory Tusks (3)\r\n== Completion==\r\nExcellent, more fine tusk specimens, though some look a bit dingy.\r\nYou have the far-reaching gratitude of the Consortium, <name>. \r\n== Gains==\r\nUpon completion of this quest you will gain:\r\n*0 [[XP]] \r\n*250 [[reputation]] with [[The Consortium]]",},
			["More Magic & Mayhem"] = { content = "#redirect [[More Magic and Mayhem]]", redirect = "More Magic and Mayhem",},
			["More Magic and Mayhem"] = { content = "'''More Magic and Mayhem''' is a source book for the [[World of Warcraft RPG]] and was published in 2005.\r\nAlso see:\r\n*",},
			["More Obsidian Warbeads"] = { content = "'''More Obsidian Warbeads''' is the repeatable version of the quest Obsidian Warbeads.\r\n==Objectives==\r\nHave you obtained any more warbeads? You'll find plenty of [[ogre]]s to the far north, near the border with [[Zangarmarsh]].\r\nYou will need:\r\n* Obsidian Warbeads x10\r\n==Details==\r\nObsidian Warbeads drop from any of the ogres throughtout [[Nagrand]].\r\n==Reward==\r\nYou will receive: 38 silver copper \r\n==Completion==\r\nWe'll make a good profit on these, <name>. I'll make sure Khoraazi hears about your work here.\r\n==Quest progression==\r\n* Obsidian Warbeads\r\n** More Obsidian Warbeads",},
			["More Skulls For Brew"] = { content = "==Progress==\r\nThe plague cauldron bubbles and churns its toxic brew, spewing a thick gas all around.\r\nDo you have more [[Scarlet Crusade|Crusader]] skulls to place inside?\r\n* Crusader Skull: (20)\r\n==Rewards==\r\nYou will receive: Noth's Special Brew\r\n==Notes==\r\nMore Noth's Special Brew! Yay!",},
			["More Spinal Dust"] = { content = "==Objectives==\r\nYou've procured more spinal dust? I can use as much of it as you bring me. \r\n*Spinal Dust (10)\r\n== Completion==\r\nThis dust is as potent as ever, <name>. Keep bringing it to me if you're in need to boost your magical powers against the Scourge. \r\n== Gains==\r\n*500 [[reputation]] with [[Tranquillien]] \r\n \r\n==Notes==\r\nThis is a repeatable quest. It is not possible to have this quest in your questbook. The questgiver has a blue ? when only the two repeatable quests are available.",},
			["More Thorium Widgets"] = { content = "==Objectives==\r\n<name>, you have been so good to us, bringing me goods\r\nwithout tiring. You have my eternal thanks!\r\nAlthough our need for Thorium widgets is not as great as\r\nit was, you may still bring them to me and I will gladly\r\ntrade them for Darkmoon Faire tickets. \r\n* Thorium Widget (6)\r\n== Completion==\r\nHere you are, <name>. Here are Darkmoon Faire\r\ntickets for your enjoyment. Do not, as they\r\nsay, spend them all in one place! \r\n== Reward==\r\n* 20x Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\r\n==Notes==\r\nSee [[Darkmoon Faire|Darkmoon Faire Reputation]] for details of this quest's availability.",},
			["Morgala Darksquall"] = { content = "Morgala Darksquall was a powerful [[naga]] [[siren]].\r\nMorgala and her warriors attacked [[Varian Wrynn]], [[Broll Bearmantle]] and [[Valeera Sanguinar]] while they were traveling on the [[Wavecutter]], [[Jaina Proudmoore]]'s private vessel. At first the naga [[myrmidon]]s were losing from the companions but then Morgala summoned a giant [[couatl]] with her magical trident. However, Valeera took the trident, consuming vast magical power from it. Meanwhile, Varian killed the couatl, which was spitting venom, and engaged Morgala herself. He then had a glimpse of his lost memory, seeing the Morgala's naga attacking him and the [[Defias]] capturing him. In his fury, he cleaved Morgala in two, the rest of her warriors fleeing.",},
			["Morgan's Plot"] = { content = "'''Morgan's Plot''' is a small church with a cemetery and a [[crypt]] located in [[Deadwind Pass]]. It can be found behind [[Karazhan]], and its graveyard is the respawn/[[Spirit Healer]] point for anyone dying within the actual [[Karazhan]] instance.\r\nThe church is inhabited by two [[Unliving Resident]]s, and there is a third patrolling just down the hill. If you get attacked, running down into the [[Crypt]] will save you.",},
			["Morgan's Vigil"] = { content = "'''Morgan's Vigil''' is an [[Alliance]] settlement in the southeastern corner of [[Burning Steppes]]. It is only a small village left in ruins; with houses and structures burned to the ground and a watch tower all crumbled and destroyed, but there are several vendors and quest givers inhabiting the small outpost. Several tents have been erected for the inhabitants to live in. Several of the quests given here involve [[Blackrock Depths]] and [[Blackrock Spire]].\r\nWhoever Morgan is or was, he is not present at the camp.\r\nBuildings: \r\n2 one storey houses (destroyed)\r\n1 Mage Tower (destroyed)\r\n3 Tents\r\n===Flight===\r\n [[Stormwind City]]\r\n [[Lakeshire]]\r\n [[Nethergarde Keep]]\r\n [[Thorium Point]]",},
			["Morganth"] = { content = "'''Morganth''' is a level 26 [[human]] [[warlock]] found in the [[Tower of Ilgalar]], [[Redridge Mountains]].\r\n==Lore==\r\nLong ago, three [[mage]]s studied in the [[mage]] tower of [[Stormwind]] until one, Morganth, fell to the dark arts. He was urged to turn away from that evil magic, but he could not resist. And so he was banished, but he took with him [[Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic]], a powerful book. The mages of Stormwind want to have that book returned because they fear that Morganth may find a way to open it and read its contents.\r\nMorganth is also a constant rival of [[Theocritus]]. He now searches for the [[Scythe of Elune]], or may even have already found it. If he has, then the Redridge Mountains and the kingdom of Stormwind will soon feel his dark might.\r\nThe [[Shadowhide Gnolls]] are his servants. The pendants that they carry allow them to communicate with their master, Morganth. Judging by artifacts found in Tower of Ilgalar, Morganth's main interest - apart from subduing local Gnoll tribes - is research on [[Dragon]]s.\r\n==Attacks and Abilities==\r\nIn combat, he is able to summon a [[succubus]] and a huge [[abomination]] to fight on his side. He is also protected by 2 Shadowhide Darkweavers. He also uses [[Fireball]] and [[Demon Armor]].\r\n==Objective of==\r\n*Drops Pendant of Shadow for the quest Morganth.",},
			["Morgan Ladimore"] = { content = "'''Morgan Ladimore''' was a soldier of [[Grand Hamlet]] (now known as [[Darkshire]]) who participated in the [[Third War]]. As he went to help fight in [[Lordaeron]], his homeland was laid waste. When he returned from the war Morgan could not find his wife [[Lys Ladimore|Lys]] nor their children. He went mad, and in his madness killed several innocents. When he came to, he saw what had come to pass and committed suicide. His body was reanimated and became an [[undead]] monstrosity known as [[Mor'Ladim]], who once roamed near [[Raven Hill]] and killed indiscriminately.\r\n==The Story of Morgan Ladimore==\r\n ''Taken from a [[The Story of Morgan Ladimore|tome]] that is given in his quest line.''\r\n'''Morgan Ladimore''' was a great and noble knight who fought in defense of the innocent, the poor, and the afflicted. For many years, he worked diligently throughout the outlying areas of [[Azeroth]], bringing relief to the suffering and swift justice to evildoers.\r\nHe was married to a young girl named Lys in the summer of his eighteenth year. They were much in love with each other and would eventually produce three children, a son and two daughters.\r\nMorgan was thirty-two when war broke out in [[Lordaeron]]. Morgan was called to the side of the legendary paladin [[Uther Lightbringer|Uther the Lightbringer]] to fight against the orcs and the undead. Leaving his wife and children in the safety of his home, Morgan left for war.\r\nThe years passed and the war dragged on, and Morgan would witness many horrific events, including the disbanding of the [[Order of the Silver Hand|Paladins of the Silver Hand]], the death of Uther and the spread of the [[Plague of Undeath|plague]]. The only thing that kept him from the brink of madness was the knowledge that he would someday be reunited with his wife and children.\r\nMorgan would eventually return to his homeland, but find it nothing like how he remembered it. The once verdant forest was corrupted and teemed with the undead and other dark forces. Destroyed houses and farms could be found everywhere, and the cemetery near Raven's Hill now dominated much of the area. A shocked and bewildered Morgan eventually made his way to his home, only to find it in ruins. Not knowing what had befallen his homeland, he headed towards the village to find answers, and, he hoped, his wife and children.\r\nMorgan inquired about his family, but could not find any answers. A priest in [[Darkshire]], as it was now called, said that he might search the cemetery at [[Raven Hill]] for a gravestone. Morgan refused to believe that his family was dead, and continued to search every farm and house in Duskwood, but to no avail.\r\nMorgan rode from Darkshire to nearby [[Lakeshire]], thinking that perhaps his family had fled. On his way there, he decided, against his better judgement, to stop by the Raven Hill cemetery. Morgan spent hours walking amongst the gravestones. He recognized many names of people that he knew and became more and more distraught. Then he saw them: a small, untended plot amongst the many with three small gravestones. A feeling of dread washed over him as he approached. Morgan brushed off the dust of the most prominent gravestone to reveal the name on it. Simply carved upon the grave, letters spelled out his worst fear:\r\nLys Ladimore\r\nBeloved Wife and Mother\r\nMorgan's apprehension turned to dismay and then to grief, and he fell to his knees weeping. For hours he stared at that one grave, begging the cold stone for forgiveness and sobbing apologies. Then, hours later, something in him snapped and he began to lash out. He brought [[Archeus|his sword]] out of its scabbard and began to rain blows on the gravestones, screaming in rage. Blind in his fury, he lashed out and swung wildly, catching the notice of a trio of the cemetery's attendants. As they turned to restrain him, he turned his focus to them, hurling accusations of guilt upon the innocent attendants, then killed them all.\r\nLater, when the rage had passed, realization crept into Morgan's mind, and he saw his bloody sword driven into the chests of one of the attendants. Driven to the brink by his emotions, he removed his belt knife and plunged it into his heart.\r\nMorgan Ladimore's body and the three bodies of his victims were found the next day. He was quickly buried, without ceremony, in a hastily dug grave on the outskirts of the cemetery. Because Morgan committed murder against innocents, something that went completely against his beliefs and his nature, and because of the grief that he held in being unable to save his family, Morgan could not die a peaceful death, and lived on as one of the restless dead.\r\nOnly days later, his grave was disturbed, and his body could not be found. The being that was Morgan now wanders Duskwood, consumed by his grief over the loss of his wife and children and his own self-hatred. [[Mor'Ladim]], as he now calls himself, roams Duskwood with mindless vengeance and hatred, and has been known to commit murder indiscriminately.\r\n==A Daughter's Love==\r\nUpon quest completion, Morgan Ladimore appears as a spirit and speaks to the player: \"My sword Archeus served me well in life, but as at last my spirit may pass from the unhappy existence, I need it no longer. I shall cling to the love of my daughter and hope that I will find forgiveness under the Light for my sins.\"\r\n==See also==\r\n*[[Ladimore|Ladimore family]]",},
			["Morgan Pestle"] = { content = "'''Morgan Pestle''' is a level 30 [[quest giver]] located in [[the Trade District]] in the [[human]] city of [[Stormwind]]. \r\nHe starts the quest Morgan's Discovery ([[Love is in the Air]]).\r\nSee [[List of Stormwind NPCs]].",},
			["Morgan the Collector"] = { content = "'''Morgan the Collector''' is a level 10 [[human]] found at the [[Brackwell Pumpkin Patch]] in [[Elwynn Forest]]. He is a member of the [[Defias Brotherhood]] and has a ring that provides clues about the connection between the [[Defias Brotherhood]] and the old [[Stonemasons]] Guild in Stormwind.\r\n[[Marshal Dughan]] wants Morgan killed.\r\n==Quests==\r\n*Manhunt\r\n==Loot==\r\n*The Collector's Ring ''(Quest Item)''",},
			["Morgroron"] = { content = "'''Morgroron''' is one of two massive pit lords found at [[Legion Hold]] in [[Shadowmoon Valley]]. He and his companion, [[Makazradon]], wield weapons crafted with powerful anti-demon enchantments intended for use against [[Illidan]].\r\nThese demons and their weapons are the subjects of the quest Capture the Weapons.\r\nHe is Immune to Warlock's Enslave Demon.",},
			["Morg Wolfsong"] = { content = "To the east of [[Thrall]]'s base known as [[Durotar]], '''Morg Wolfsong''' the [[Far Seer|far seer]] and his party of [[orc]] [[shaman]]s were attacked by [[orc]] [[warlock]]s. [[Rexxar]] and [[Rokhan]] defeated these warlocks and restored Morg Wolfsong's honor, allowing his fatally wounded body to pass away in peace.",},
			["Morin Cloudstalker"] = { content = "'''Morin Cloudstalker''' is a wandering level 10 [[quest giver]] located on the road from [[Bloodhoof Village]] to the entrance to the [[Barrens]] in the [[tauren]] starting zone of [[Mulgore]]. \r\nHe starts the following quests:\r\n* The Ravaged Caravan\r\n* The Venture Co.\r\n* Supervisor Fizsprocket\r\nSee [[List of Mulgore NPCs]].",},
			["Morja"] = { content = "'''Morja''' is a level 12 [[quest giver]] located in in the [[Darkmoon Faire]] camp, which is only available during the monthly Darkmoon Faire event. It rotates each month to a different location. One month it will be south of [[Goldshire]] in the [[human]] starting zone of [[Elwynn Forest]]. Then, it is off to [[Kalimdor]] where it is southwest of [[Thunder Bluff]] in the [[tauren]] starting zone of [[Mulgore]]. Then it travels to [[Outland]] near [[Shattrath City]]. \r\nMorja has lost Jubjub, her [[jubling]] frog, and only [[Dark Iron Ale Mug]] can get him back.\r\nShe starts the quest Spawn of Jubjub.\r\nSee [[List of Elwynn Forest NPCs]] and [[List of Mulgore NPCs]].",},
			["Morloch"] = { content = "==Information==\r\nMorloch is a Trogg champion who claims the irondeep mine at the beginning of every Alterac Valley battleground. He must be killed in order to claim the mine for your faction. He is guarded by two randomly chosen Irondeep Troggs, either [[Irondeep Shaman]] or [[Irondeep Skullthumper]].\r\n==Abilities==\r\nThe following abilities and corresponding damage reports is when Morloch is level 68.\r\n*Shadow Bolt: Takes 2 Seconds to cast, hits for around 1700.\r\n*Shadow Bolt Volley: Instant cast shadow damage, hits for around 1200.\r\n*Curse of Weakness: Reduces attack power by 51 for 2 minutes.\r\n*Has a pet imp.",},
			["Morlos'Aran"] = { content = "'''Morlos'Aran''' was once a great [[night elf]] settlement, long before the [[Great Sundering]]. It is located at the southern edge of [[Felwood]]. There are similar ruins located nearby, at [[Ameth'Aran]] and [[Bashal'Aran]] in [[Darkshore]], [[Ordil'Aran]] in [[Ashenvale]], and [[Tethris'Aran]] in [[Desolace]]. Once thriving cities, now these ruins only serve as a reminder of the golden age that was lost long ago.",},
			["Morning Glory Dew"] = { content = "==Source==\r\nThis item can be purchased for 40 silver copper from:\r\n* Joshua Maclure in [[Elwynn Forest]]\r\n* Barkeep Hann in [[Duskwood]]\r\n* Innkeeper Farley in [[Elwynn Forest]]\r\n* Barkeep Dobbins in [[Elwynn Forest]]\r\n* Corporal Bluth in [[Stranglethorn Vale]]\r\n* Sergeant De Vries in [[Elwynn Forest]]\r\n* Thultash in [[Swamp of Sorrows]]\r\n* Kazan Mogosh in [[Dun Morogh]]\r\n* Innkeeper Belm in [[Dun Morogh]]\r\n* Elly Langston in [[Stormwind City]]\r\n* Innkeeper Helbrek in [[Wetlands]]\r\n* Keeg Gibn in [[Dun Morogh]]\r\n* Lyranne Feathersong in [[Winterspring]]\r\n* Innkeeper Anderson in [[Hillsbrad Foothills]]\r\n* Neema in [[Hillsbrad Foothills]]\r\n* Barkeep Kelly in [[Hillsbrad Foothills]]\r\n* Innkeeper Shay in [[Hillsbrad Foothills]]\r\n* Nixxrax Fillamug in [[Stranglethorn Vale]]\r\n* Gretchen Vogel in [[Redridge Mountains]]\r\n* Gabrielle Chase in [[Burning Steppes]]\r\n* Denni'ka in [[Stonetalon Mountains]]\r\n* Bernie Heisten in [[Blasted Lands]]\r\n* Dalaran Brewmaster in [[Silverpine Forest]]\r\n* Kurll in [[Azshara]]\r\n* Laer Stepperunner in [[Thousand Needles]]\r\n* Gruna in [[Burning Steppes]]\r\n* Grimtak in [[Durotar]]\r\n* Zlagk in [[Durotar]]\r\n* Moodan Sungrain in [[Mulgore]]\r\n* Jhawna Oatwind in [[Mulgore]]\r\n* Innkeeper Boorand Plainswind in [[The Barrens]]\r\n* Kira Songshine in [[Elwynn Forest]]\r\n* Nantar in [[Ashenvale]]\r\n* Maliynn in [[Ashenvale]]\r\n* Dendrythis in [[Teldrassil]]\r\n* Jaeana in [[Teldrassil]]\r\n* Fyrenna in [[Teldrassil]]\r\n* Kyndri in [[Darkshore]]\r\n* Allyndia in [[Darkshore]]\r\n* Taldan in [[Darkshore]]\r\n* Tiyani in [[Darkshore]]\r\n* Brogus Thunderbrew in [[Alterac Valley]]\r\n* Danlyia in [[Teldrassil]]\r\n* Tawny Grisette in [[Tirisfal Glades]]\r\n* Eleanor Rusk in [[Tirisfal Glades]]\r\n* Morley Bates in [[Tirisfal Glades]]\r\n* Truk Wildbeard in [[The Hinterlands]]\r\n* Turhaw in [[Thousand Needles]]\r\n* Ogg'marr in [[Dustwallow Marsh]]\r\n