			["Server:Cenarion Circle"] = { content = "#REDIRECT [[Server:Cenarion Circle US]]", redirect = "Server:Cenarion Circle US",},
			["Server:Emerald Dream Europe"] = { content = "<div style=\"max-width:76em; margin: 1em auto 0px auto;\"></div>",},
			["Server:Emerald Dream US"] = { content = "The '''Emerald Dream''' server (US) is a Role-play – Player vs. Player (RPPvP) Central time zone realm. It opened in September of 2005 as one of three pioneering servers to combine [[RP|role-play]] with a [[PvP]] rule set. (There is also a [[Server:Emerald Dream Europe|European Emerald Dream PvE]] server of the same name.)\r\nRP-PvP servers were opened at subscribers’ request. Prior to the opening of this type, players had to choose between Role-play PvE servers or straight PvP servers, often splitting time between realm types to satisfy both areas of interest.\r\nThe [[Emerald Dream]] moniker (abbreviated as ED) is a reference to the idyllic natural paradise and alternate reality as envisioned and created by the dragon [[Ysera]] and thus has strong [[druid]]ic connotations.\r\n==The players==\r\nPerhaps due to the original limited release of the realm type, the Emerald Dream server has attracted, and continues to attract, players from well outside its local time zone (or the United States for that matter).\r\nThe realm has gathered to it a multitude of players with varied concentrations and emphases of interest between role-play, environmental content progression, and player verse player challenges.\r\nThe more loathed types of players are those with insufficient respect for the [[RP|role play requirements]] of the server and have simply come because they (often erroneously) believe role players to be “easy pickins”; additionally, the elitists who believe themselves (just as erroneous) privileged and bemoan the fact that someone dared kill them while they were enacting some self aggrandizing plot line. While these players are thankfully in the minority, they tend to be noticed more as their play is conspicuously poor and also tend to be quite mouthy.\r\nOf the more positive and preferred ends of the spectrum are the role-players that forgo content progression or [[PvP Rewards|PvP accolades]] and simply prefer to adventure in an environment where there is more random peril than the AI presents; and the PvPers and PvEers, while not actively participating in role play themselves, favor and respect the more immersive environment that the role play provides. These types coexist quite well. As such, the majority of players lay somewhere between these ends, and are often found cooperating as shifting interests coincide.\r\nThe denizens of the server are referred to as “Emerald Dreamers”, “Dreamers”, or simply and more commonly “EDers”.\r\n===Characters===\r\nFor more information on specific inhabitants of the realm, you can visit the [[Server:Emerald Dream US/Directory Guide|Emerald Dream Character Directory]].\r\n===Personalities===\r\nYou can read about some select colorful \"personalities\" of Emerald Dream by visiting the [[Server:Emerald Dream US/Personalities|Personalities of Emerald Dream]] page\r\n===Server Queue Times===\r\nRare. Burning Crusade introduced Queue times upwards of 10 minutes but these have dissipated and logon queue times occur rarely (once to tiwce a month) during peak hours.\r\n====Battle Ground Queue Times====\r\n*Note: these times can vary depending on the PvP Daily, what BG weekend it is, and if you are joining as a group or by yourself. The times and ratios given are an average.\r\n=====Bracket: 60-69=====\r\n*Note: The minimum level for [[Eye of the Storm]] is 61\r\n=====Bracket: 50-59=====\r\n*Note: The minimum level for [[Alterac Valley]] is 51\r\n====Arena Queue Times====\r\n*Note: these times can vary, especially throughout the day. The times given are an average.\r\n==Realm forum==\r\nSupplemental to in-game activity, the also enjoys lively participation and is often viewed as an extension of the game if not a game unto itself.\r\nDue to a mix of interests, creativity, and strong personalities, the forum is a volatile brew of smack talk, game mechanic discussion, mindless banter, playing tips, laments, citations of good play, jibes, song and movie quotes, jingoism, bon mots, insults, role play and creative writing.\r\nNaturally, with a server emphasis on role play, the more popular posts tend to be of the role playing and creative writing ilk. Styles and subject matter range considerably from complete game inspired fantasy fiction, to role play re-tellings of in-game events, to satiric interpretations of real life expressed in game terms.\r\nIn an effort to give roleplayers on Emerald Dream a more hospitable forum environment, the has been created. Fellow ED roleplayers are encouraged to participate in this fun and growing community.\r\n===Notable forum trolls===\r\nThen again, everybody loves a good quip, as evinced by the healthy and “renown” population of that call the place home.\r\nYou can read about some of our more infamous trolls on the [[Server:Emerald Dream US/Trolls|Notable Forum Trolls]] page.\r\n==Guilds==\r\nGuilds on Emerald Dream are as diverse as it characters, with different levels of interest in Role-play, PvE and PvP.\r\nFor descriptions of active and defunct guilds and their interests, see the \r\n=====[[Server:Emerald Dream US/Horde Guilds|Horde Guild List]]=====\r\nFor guild progression, see the \r\n==Realm History==\r\nMajor events in the realm’s past including server firsts, faction boss kills, significant RP-PvP events, and earth shattering conflicts can be viewed on the [[Server:Emerald Dream US/Realm History|Realm History]] page.",},
			["Server:Ghostlands US"] = { content = "'''Ghostlands US''' was opened on January 31, 2008 as destination realm during the of late January/early February '08 and is the newest member of the [[Battlegroup US Retaliation|Retaliation]] [[battlegroup]].\r\n==Ghostlands Resources==\r\n* \r\n* [[Server:Ghostlands US/Guild Progression|Guild Progression]]\r\n* [[Server:Ghostlands US/Rare Crafting|Crafting]]\r\n==Important Information==\r\nGhostlands consists of an equal 1:1 Horde to Alliance ratio. The server is in dire need of raiding guilds and powerful arena teams, so transfers of higher levels are reccomended for this newer server. While many new characters are being made, more are needed for a larger and more unbalanced ratio (as most successful realms are). 8000 to 8100 Alliance versus Horde.\r\n==Seed Realms==\r\nAlthough Ghostlands is now open to new character creation and paid character transfers, it initially consisted of solely of transferring characters from the following realms:\r\n* Aerie Peak\r\n* Aggramar\r\n* Alexstrasza\r\n* Alleria\r\n* Argent Dawn\r\n* Blackhand\r\n* Cenarius\r\n* Doomhammer\r\n* Hellscream\r\n* Whisperwind \r\n==Players== \r\nShiromar was the 1st SL,HA,CN,JS,OTSS titled player to transfer into Ghostlands June 19 2008.\r\nWeevenge was the first player to down Hogger. He also declared himself the King of Ghostlands.\r\nEPICS FTW was the first guild to have the bank ganked and disbanded.\r\nThere is also a well known warrior by the name of Picklebus, who fashions himself some sort of leader, of a new republic.",},
			["Server:Hyjal US"] = { content = "Server (Realm) Name: Hyjal \r\nServer Type: [[PvE]] \r\nServer Location (physical): [[:Category:Pacific Time Zone servers|US, Pacific]] \r\n*Hyjal is part of Battlegroup 11\r\n=Realm News=\r\nFor realm news &amp; discussion, see .\r\n=Hyjal Guild Progression=\r\n==Tier 6 Progression==\r\n Guild [BT- ICMRGTASN] [HS- AZKNW]\r\n 1. H Forgotten Aspects Aug 20 2007 Aug 06 2007\r\n 2. A Casual Oct 01 2007 Aug 13 2007\r\n 3. H Advent Fury 4/9 ** 4/5 **\r\n A Lethality 4/9 ** 4/5 **\r\n'''''-- LEGEND --'''''\r\n'''BT: ''Black Temple''' (in progression order)''\r\n*I -- Illidan Stormrage\r\n*C -- Illidari Council\r\n*M -- Mother Shahraz\r\n*R -- Reliquary of Souls\r\n*G -- Gurtogg Bloodboil\r\n*T -- Teron Gorefiend\r\n*A -- Shade of Akama\r\n*S -- Supremus\r\n*N -- High Warlord Naj'entus\r\n'''HS: ''Hyjal Summit''' (in progression order)''\r\n*A -- Archimonde\r\n*Z -- Azgalor\r\n*K -- Kaz'rogal\r\n*N -- Anetheron\r\n*W -- Rage Winterchill\r\nThe guild(s) above all completed Tier 4&5 Progression (through Serpentshrine Cavern and Tempest Keep: Eye)\r\n==Tier 4/5 Progression==\r\n Guild [TKE KSAV] [SSC VMHLKB] [Mag][Gru] [DLK][DWk] [Kar]\r\n H Forgotten Aspects Jun 24 2007 May 31 2007 * * * * *\r\n A Casual Jul 11 2007 Jun 10 2007 * * * * *\r\n A Lethality Aug 15 2007 Jul 16 2007 * * * * *\r\n H Advent Fury Aug 17 2007 Jun 29 2007 * * * * *\r\n H Tsunami 3/4 ** Jul 22 2007 * * * * *\r\n A Cry Havoc 3/4 ** Sep 06 2007 * * *\r\n A Driven 3/4 ** Sep 28 2007 * * *\r\n H Avarice 3/4 ** 5/6 *** * * * * *\r\n H The Fabled 3/4 ** 5/6 *** * * * * *\r\n A Kriegsherren 1/4 * 5/6 *** * * * * *\r\n A Erebus 1/4 * 4/6 ** * * * * *\r\n A Crisis 2/6 * * * * *\r\n H Cynical 1/4 * 1/6 * * * * *\r\n A The Company 1/4 * 1/6 * * * *\r\n A The Eternal 1/4 * 1/6 * * * *\r\n A Sarcastic & Drunk 1/4 * 1/6 * * * *\r\n H Smile 1/4 * * *\r\n A Fusion 1/4 * * * *\r\n A Chaos 1/4 * * *\r\n A Adversary 1/4 * * *\r\n A Devil Theory * * *\r\n A Eximius Gens * *\r\n H Explorers * *\r\n A Apocalypse Legion * *\r\n H The Ides of March * *\r\n H Angli Vel Angelus * *\r\n H Echoes of Immortal * *\r\n H Rage * *\r\n A Halcyon * *\r\n H Serenity * *\r\n H Burning Sensation * *\r\n A Free Booters * *\r\n A Trivial * *\r\n A On the Bounty * *\r\n H Spiritual Machines * *\r\n A Vox Noctis * *\r\n H Dark Revenant * *\r\n A Eclipse * *\r\n A The Infinite * *\r\n A Bellum Gero M *\r\n H Riven * *\r\n H Veracity *\r\n A Honorbound *\r\n A Zombies Ate My *\r\n A Ruthless *\r\n A Persecution *\r\n A Conspiracy *\r\n A Relevance *\r\n A Bonzo Dog Doo *\r\n \r\n'''''-- LEGEND --'''''\r\n'''TKE: ''The Eye- Tempest Keep''' (in ranking order)''\r\n*K -- Kael'thas Sunstrider\r\n*S -- High Astromancer Solarian\r\n*A -- Al'ar -Phoenix God-\r\n*V -- Void Reaver\r\n'''SSC: ''Serpentshrine Cavern''' (in ranking order)''\r\n*V -- Lady Vashj\r\n*M -- Morogrim Tidewalker\r\n*H -- Hydross the Unstable\r\n*L -- Leotheras the Blind\r\n*K -- Fathom-Lord Karathress\r\n*B -- The Lurker Below\r\n'''Mag: ''Magtheridon'''''\r\n'''Gru: ''Gruul's Lair'''''\r\n*M -- High King Maulgar\r\n'''DLK: ''Doom Lord Kazzak'''''\r\n'''DWk: ''Doomwalker'''''\r\n'''Kar: ''Karazhan''' -only tracking Nightbane kills-''\r\nLast Updated: 10/3/07 @10:30am PST\r\n==Recognizable / Legendary Players==\r\n*Mcdoc - The Chief Medical Officer abord the starship Hyjal.\r\n==Realm News==\r\nHyjal is a bustling server with an equal balance of Horde and Ally.\r\n===Enchanting===\r\n{| border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"1\" cellpadding=\"2\" style=\"margin: 1em auto 1em auto\" width=\"100%\"",},
			["Server:Kel'Thuzad Europe"] = { content = "===Forums===\r\n*",},
			["Server:Kel'Thuzad US"] = { content = "'''Kel'Thuzad''' is one of the original 43 [[PvP]] servers that were opened upon the release of World of Warcraft, and is named after the lich [[Kel'Thuzad]]. The server runs at Mountain Standard Time.\r\nThe realm has a player base intensely active in both PVE and PVP play and currently has an Alliance to Horde ratio of approximately 3.2:1. This causes some balance issues in world PvP and events, such as . \r\n==History==\r\nKel'Thuzad has a long history of server issues and high population. Months of crashes, lag, and downtime were mostly resolved when the server was transferred to a new hardware cluster. Kel'Thuzad has remained a high population server since its launch, despite several periods where Blizzard opened free character transfers off of the server.\r\nSome notable events in Kel'Thuzad's history include:\r\n* scored a on M'uru, putting Kel'thuzad back on the map for PVE progression. They also put out one of the first videos for it. They also were the fifth guild world wide to kill Kil'jaden in TBC.\r\n*A Pick-up group (Horde Side) which formed multiple times a week under the leadership of Shiektal successfully defeated all of Blackwing Lair and Ahn'Qiraj 40 up to C'thun's trash mobs every week. Nearly 100 players showed up weekly to the meeting spot to get an invite.\r\n*Opening the gates of Ahn'Qiraj. Kel'Thuzad was one of the first 30 servers (and the 11th PVP server) to open the gates.\r\n*Horde players from the guild Fortis kited [Kazzak the Supreme|Lord Kazzak] from the Blasted Lands into Stormwind City. This led to a hotfix by Blizzard preventing kiting Kazzak.\r\n*Massive PVP zergs in the Hillsbrad Foothills after the implementation of the honor system which included more than 400 players.\r\n*The and guilds teaming to kill Onyxia for the first time on the server. Their videos (including a ) and strategies were studied by thousands of other WoW players.\r\n*Several multi-guild attacks on the leaders of capital cities launched by both Alliance and Horde. The attacks involved hundreds of players. Which lead to numerous server crashes from both factions raiding cities.\r\n*The legendary Vidas by lvl 29 alts from Fortis.\r\n==Kel'Thuzad [[Guild]]s==\r\nDetailed Kel'Thuzad guild progression tables can be found [[Server:Kel'Thuzad US/Guild Progression| here]].\r\n==Rank 14 PvPers==\r\nThese are all of the players who obtained the ranks of Grand Marshal and High Warlord under the original honor system.",},
			["Server:Khaz Modan US"] = { content = "==\"Khaz Modan\" in WoW Lore==\r\n[[Khaz Modan]] is the mountainous kingdom of the [[Ironforge Clan]], ruled by the [[Bronzebeard Clan]], founded after the awakened [[dwarf|dwarves]] ventured out from the ancient city of [[Uldaman]]. Named the \"Mountain or Mountains of Khaz\" after the [[Titan]] shaper [[Khaz'goroth]], thought to be the creator of the dwarven race. The kingdom is ruled from the great underground city of [[Ironforge]]. Khaz Modan is also the name of the continent in which the kingdom is located, comprised of [[Dun Morogh]], [[Loch Modan]], the [[Wetlands]], and the [[Badlands]]. The mountains here are also called the Khaz Mountains.\r\n==General Information==\r\nKhaz Modan is a World of Warcraft US PvE Realm located in the '''Central Standard Time zone'''. The server went live in January, 2006. As of October, 2007, its population includes approximately 17,000 active characters above level ten, with a faction ratio of roughly 1.7:1 (Alliance: Horde).\r\nKhaz Modan is still young compared to other servers in the matter of content progression and player base, but it has a close community and welcoming player environment. The majority of the realm's end-game guilds are hybrid guilds that promote both social interaction and raid progress. Only three Khaz Modan Alliance guilds, Infamous(330), Authority(463), and Sunder(589), have ranked in the top six hundred World of Warcraft US raiding guilds as of August, 2008, according to .(Scoundrels(1020) is the top horde guild; ranking in nearly the top thousand)\r\n'''Official Realm Forum:''' \r\n===Population and Activity===\r\n'''Most active guild:''' Tempting Fate since August, 2008.\r\n'''Top Alliance guilds by level and activity:'''\r\n*1. Veritas\r\n*2. Herismo\r\n*3. Vanguard of War\r\n'''Top Horde guilds by level and activity:'''\r\n*1. Tempting Fate\r\n*2. Aurora\r\n*3. Cruoris\r\n'''August, 2008'''\r\n*Total characters: 18,803\r\n** 12,873 (69%)\r\n** 5,930 (32%)\r\n*** vs Ratio: '''2.2:1''' \r\n*** vs Activity Ratio: '''2.2:1'''\r\n'''October, 2007'''\r\n*Total characters: 17,000 \r\n** 10,800 (64%)\r\n** 6,200 (36%)\r\n*** vs Ratio: '''1.7:1''' \r\n*** vs Activity Ratio: '''2.4:1'''\r\n''Source:, accurate as of 14 August, 2008, but should be considered '''strictly informational'''.'' ''Please help maintain accurate information by submitting data for this realm! Find out more about how to help here: \r\n==Khaz Modan Raid Progression==\r\nAs of October 2008, the top three raiding guilds according to continue to be:\r\n*1. Infamous \r\n*2. Authority \r\n*3. Sunder \r\nHowever, due to WowJutsu's current discrepancy, as of October 2008 (Post Patch 3.0), the top three raiding guilds are:\r\n*1. Sunder \r\n*2. Authority \r\n*3. Scoundrels \r\n===Sites for Tracking KM Raid Progression===\r\n*\r\n*[[Server:Khaz Modan US/Guild Progression]]\r\n===Pre-TBC Raid History===\r\nA small number of guilds transfered to Khaz Modan when the realm went live, including Sunder, Vision, DarkSin, Skunk Canyon Brigade, and the founders of the guild Scoundrels. Before the expansion The Burning Crusade was released in January, 2007, these guilds led Khaz Modan raid progression.\r\nHaving already cleared [[Blackwing_Lair|Blackwing Lair]], the Alliance guild Sunder stood as the furthest progressing guild in Player vs Environment content, getting many \"server firsts\" by default. They continue to be the top guild on Khaz Modan, having been the first to down many bosses in content released since their transfer.\r\nSunder continued to lead the pack in instance progression, having downed C'thun in [[Temple_of_Ahn'Qiraj|AQ40]] on December 3, 2006, and cleared the Spider Wing of [[Naxxramas]]. A significant number of other Alliance guilds have also completed the content of [[Molten_core|MC]], [[Blackwing_Lair|BWL]], and [[Onyxia's_Lair|Onyxia]].\r\nScoundrels lead the Horde in PvE content and were working on downing C'Thun and progressing in Naxxramas. Retribution followed close behind, with Onyxia, MC, and BWL completed.\r\n===Legendaries on Khaz Modan===\r\nThunderfury, Blessed Blade of the Windseeker is wielded on the Alliance side by Gunnarr <Sunder>, Katay <Veni Vidi Vici>, Dinghy <Authority>, Infekted <Prestige> and Fenz. Thunderfury wielders for Horde side are Hellhawk <Sons of Thanatos>. Currently, (A)Dyncaus <Art of War>, and (H)Mooebird <Retribution> have one of the bracers needed for Thunderfury.\r\nSulfuras, Hand of Ragnaros is owned on the Horde side by Astayld <Blind Fate> and Zumii <Retribution>. Sulfuras is wielded on the Alliance side by Doff <Sunder>, Taurenpriest, Rodomir <Prestige>, Shalashaska <Vision>, Bainstoneaxe <Calamitously Caffeinated>, Rigel and Stikman <Authority>.\r\nAtiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian is wielded on the Alliance side by Kinien <Sunder>.\r\nWarglaive of Azzinoth is wielded on the Alliance side by Lightstar <Sunder> (Both), Niroth <Sunder> (Both), Lanette <Soul> (Main Hand), Shayleigh <Soul> (MH), Ukier <The Elitists> (MH), Xcorp <Vision> (MH), and Esten <Evil Doers> (Off Hand). Both are wielded on the Horde side by Nyllith <Scoundrels>.\r\nBlack Qiraji Resonating Crystal is owned on the Alliance side by Selinar <Onomatopoeia>.\r\n==Player vs. Player==\r\nPlayer vs. Player combat did not exist at all during the first month of the realm's existence - a player would be lucky to have at least one battleground match a day. Out of frustration the Alliance would lay siege to Orgrimmar or the Crossroads in a attempt to get their PvP fix. \r\nOver time PvP became more frequent in the Khaz Modan community. Players would face off with other players from the opposing faction and destroy one another.\r\n===Patch 1.12 and PvP===\r\n[[1.12|Patch 1.12]] introduced cross realm battlegrounds. This allowed players from several different realms to come together for battlegrounds and reduced queue times tremendously. Before patch 1.12 it was common to wait for hours to get into a BG, but now queue times are often non-existent or a matter of minutes. Khaz Modan is a member of Battlegroup Vengeance.\r\n===Patch 2.0 and PvP===\r\nOn December 5th 2006, [[Patch_2.0.1_Release_Notes|server patch 2.0.1]] was released and introduced the new honor reward system. This new reward system allows players to accumulate honor points that can be spent like currency to purchase weapons, armor, and various other items beneficial for player-vs-player progression. The rankings no longer exist with this new system. The last players on Khaz Modan to reach Rank 14 were Ixnay (Alliance) and Wanagetdrunc (Horde).\r\nThe following players achieved Rank 14 (Grand Marshal) for the Alliance on the Khaz Modan server:\r\nSdotkilla,\r\nDevildwarf (now Dorfalicious),\r\nSaidas,\r\nLunchlady,\r\nBarea,\r\nBru,\r\nNitrowarrior,\r\nNitezstalka,\r\nBowlduster,\r\nLykann,\r\nJomamma (transferred to Blackhand),\r\nAedan,\r\nLightstar,\r\nWickedwonda\r\nThe following players achieved Rank 14 (High Warlord) for the Horde on the Khaz Modan server:\r\nMaurana,\r\nMizery,\r\nWanagetdrunc,\r\nFuroc,\r\nQuaid\r\nPlease add if you know any information.\r\n==Server History==\r\nKhaz Modan was the name given to Realm Number 86. This realm was created to help alleviate the growing populations of other servers which were becoming increasingly over crowded with log in queue times up to 30 minutes. Blizzard blamed this on the growing population from the 2005 Holiday shopping season. On January 3, 2006, Khaz Modan went live.\r\nKhaz Modan was specifically set up to allow transfers from four well-established realms:\r\n* [[Server:Blackhand US|Blackhand]]\r\n* [[Server:Draka US|Draka]]\r\n* [[Server:Hellscream US|Hellscream]]\r\n* [[Server:Proudmoore US|Proudmoore]]\r\nDuring the first weeks after Khaz Modan went live there was not a lot of community activity. Cities were empty, battles between the Horde and the Alliance in the battlegrounds did not exist. Some were afraid that after they transfered they made a mistake due to the emptiness players felt when exploring Azeroth. However many players also enjoyed the wide open space and lag free major cities.\r\nThe population grew slowly but steadily, reaching a record high of nearly 20,000 active characters above level ten by July, 2007.\r\n===Server Hardware Retrofit===\r\nOn Tuesday, September 19th, 2006, the server was taken down along with a group of servers for new hardware upgrades. The server was down for 36 hours, and noted results have been lag improvements and smoother game play.\r\n===The Gates of Ahn'Qiraj: Patch 1.9 Unleashed===\r\nCoincidently this Patch went live the same day that the Khaz Modan server went live. During the Opening of the Ahn`Qiraj Gate, the Alliance guild Sunder led both sides in the war effort to get these gates open as soon as possible and was also the guild that rang the gong to open the gates.\r\nOn February 28th, 2006, the Gates were opened by Elmiser of Sunder, and Ahn'Qiraj became available to the people of Khaz Modan. Khaz Modan was the 83rd realm to complete the War Effort.\r\n[[C'Thun]], the final boss of AQ40, was first killed by the Alliance guild Sunder on December 3, 2006.",},
			["Server:Kilrogg US"] = { content = "<div style=\"max-width:70em; margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto;\">\r\n</div>\r\n__NOEDITSECTION__",},
			["Server:Lightbringer US"] = { content = "Server (Realm) Name: Lightbringer \r\nServer Type: [[PvE]] \r\nServer Location (physical): [[:Category:Pacific Time Zone servers|US, Pacific]] \r\n* Lightbringer is part of Battlegroup 11\r\n==Guilds on Server \"Lightbringer\"==\r\nGuilds of this Realm, and links to more information about the listed guild.\r\n==== [[Alliance]]====\r\n*[[Guild:Affliction (Lightbringer US) |Affliction]]: \r\n*Age of Wisdom: \r\n*Blood Blades\r\n*[[Guild:Blood in the Streets (Lightbringer US) |Blood in the Streets]]: \r\n*[[Guild:Bloodpack (Lightbringer US) |Bloodpack]]: \r\n*Centered: \r\n*Clan Canada \r\n*Crescent: \r\n*Dark Legacy: \r\n*Disavowed: \r\n*Elite Vanguard: \r\n*Elysian Conclave: \r\n*Eternal Reign: \r\n*Final Ascension: \r\n*Immortal: \r\n*[[Guild:Fluffy Bunnies of_Doom (Lightbringer US)|Fluffy Bunnies of Doom]]: \r\n*[[Guild:Bloody Demonic Legion (Lightbringer US) |Bloody Demonic Legion]]:\r\n*Outcasts: \r\n*[[Guild:The Naked Brigade (Lightbringer US) |The Naked Brigade]]: \r\n*Forgiven: \r\n*S U P E RV I L L I A N S: \r\n*[[Guild:Not Ðead Yet (Lightbringer US) |Not Ðead Yet]] : \r\n==== [[Horde]]====\r\n*Ashen Souls: \r\n*Bad Moon Rising: \r\n*Exlortum: \r\n*Hells Syndicate: \r\n*iKoA: \r\n*Menagerie: \r\n*Oryx: \r\n*Outcasts Reborn: \r\n*Phoenix Arisen: \r\n*Rosemarys Babies: \r\n*Scenites: \r\n*Silent Reality: \r\n*The Scourge: \r\n*Thundering Hoard: ?\r\n*Tupan Techno: \r\n*Vorpal Rabbits: \r\n*Wicked Intentions: \r\n==Realm News==\r\nFor realm news &amp; discussion, see .\r\n==SUPER VILLIANS INVADE!==\r\nIn the early morning hours of Sunday, August 24th 2008, 4 evil super villians escaped from Arkham Asylum and infiltrated Lightbringer, creating alliance characters on the realm! The villians terrorized trade chat for hours, striking fear into the hearts of the alliance! After they were finished, they retreated to their lair beneath Ironforge to await a new day to once again foil the plans of the super heroes and to generally cause mayhem!",},
			["Server:Magtheridon Europe"] = { content = "==Information==\r\nThis server is an english [[PvP]] [[realm|server]].\r\nIf you plan on editing this page in some way, leave a note on the [[Server_Talk:Magtheridon Europe|Mag Discussion]] page, or at the History page. Make sure to sign your name on the Discussion page, using the format --~~~~.\r\n===Links===\r\n*\r\n*\r\n===IRC===\r\n[irc://irc.quakenet.org/magtheridon #magtheridon at quakenet]\r\n===Crafters and Enchanters===\r\nSee [[Server:Magtheridon Europe/Crafting Index|Magtheridon Europe/Crafting Index]] for crafted items, and [[Server:Magtheridon Europe/Enchants|Magtheridon Europe/Enchants]] for enchants. For the pre-TBC equivalents, see [[Server:Magtheridon Europe/Pre-BC Crafting|Magtheridon Europe/Pre-BC Crafting]] and [[Server:Magtheridon Europe/Pre-BC Crafting|Magtheridon Europe/Pre-BC Crafting]].\r\n===Progression===\r\nPre-TBC raid progress can be found [[Server:Magtheridon Europe/Guild Raid Progress|here]]. Source: \r\n====10 & 25 Man Raid Progression====\r\nSource:",},
			["Server:Medivh US"] = { content = "'''Medivh''' is an original release, [[PvE]] server in the eastern standard timezone, Medivh has been one of the more notable servers for its guilds' progression through raid instances and world events.\r\n====Overview====\r\nUpon the original release of the game, the horde guild <Ascent> claimed the world first kill of [[Ragnaros]], the final boss in [[Molten Core]]. Later with the introduction of [[Blackwing Lair]], the [[Alliance]] guild <Fury> was the first in the world to down four of the seven bosses in the instance -- [[Broodlord Lashlayer]], [[Firemaw]], [[Ebonroc]], and [[Flamegor]].\r\n====Gates of Ahn'Qiraj Event====\r\nWith the release of [[Patch 1.9 (Release Notes)|Patch 1.9]], the ''[[Gates of Ahn'Qiraj]]'' Medivh quickly organized its forces and succeeded in being the first server in the world to complete the world event and open the gates. This was done by massive cross-faction co-operation initiated by <Ascent> and joined by the vast majority of the high end scene on the server. Due to the significant numerical differences between horde and alliance (3-4 alliance per 1 horde) <Ascent> agreed to let <Fury> finish the scepter. With a portion of alliance focusing on the scepter, the progress between the two factions was equalized significantly. Even with this, it became obvious that alliance would finish significantly ahead of horde unless something was done. The solution was to funnel materials from alliance to horde, with the horde side funnel end points all being in <Ascent> and alliance side end points being in <Fury>, <The Transcendent>, <Heroic Few> and some other alliance guilds.\r\nThe leader of <Fury>, a [[dwarf]] [[warrior]] named Kalahad, was the bearer of the [[Scepter of the Shifting Sands]] who officially unlocked the gate. During this period, the server population was swelled by a flood of low level alternate characters created by players from other servers for various reasons -- including to get to Silithus to be able to view the gate opening, and to attempt to force Medivh to the population max so that the regular members of the server would be unable to log in to help with the war effort. In an attempt to reduce the number of characters in Kalimdor, and specifically Silithus before the gate was opened, the high end guilds coordinated to raid all the major locations in the hopes of drawing people to defend them. However, despite their efforts, and Blizzard's attempt to reinforce the server hardware, the server crashed several times before and after the gate was opened. Several players present when Kalahad rang the Scarab Gong reported that the world server crashed at the very moment the gong was struck.\r\nUpon the opening of the gates, Medivh's endgame raiding guilds led the way into the [[Temple of Ahn'Qiraj]] where <Fury> claimed the world first kills of [[The Prophet Skeram]], Vem, [[Fankriss the Unyielding]], and [[Princess Huhuran]]. <Ascent> claimed Lord Kri, but got stalled at Sartura who was tuned horribly at this point (<Fury> simply jumped over her). Unfortunately the original explorers of the zone were rewarded with numerous revamps and changes in the encounters, which made the early experiences nearly useless. These problems materialized most of all with C'Thun, which <Fury> would probably have killed first had it not needed so significant changes to be killable.\r\n====Overpopulation====\r\nThe server population has remained high ever since the Ahn'Qiraj event, and the server had still had the original release hardware. As a result, many guilds progressing through Molten Core, Blackwing Lair, Ahn'Qiraj, and now [[Naxxramas]] have been severely hindered by recurrent lag spikes and high latency. \r\nAs a result, with the introduction of cross-server transfers, two leading Horde guilds, <Ascent> and <Vindication>, transferred off the server. Almost immediately after they transferred off the server, the server hardware was updated.\r\n====Feud with Mannoroth====\r\nDuring the race for Ahn'Qiraj, a rivalry was ignited with the [[Server:Mannoroth|Mannoroth server]], the first PvP server and second overall to complete the event. The race to complete the war effort was neck-and-neck for some time. In an effort to gain an advantage for their home server, players from Medivh and Mannoroth created alts on the opposing server to increase lag and queue times. Players also trolled the realm forums of the opposing server, trading insults like \"carebear\" and \"Mannorofl\".\r\nThough Medivh emerged victorious, some Mannoroth players still claim they were the first \"legitimate\" server to complete the event, as Medivh's PvE mechanics prevented cross-faction interference and made organization between Horde and Alliance a natural course of action. By contrast, Mannoroth's war effort was hindered throughout the event by fierce competition between Horde and Alliance Scepter quest raids. Ganking in Silithus ignited a no-holds-barred war between the factions, causing constant server crashes due to zone overpopulation and ending in a battle at the Scarab Gong.\r\nMost Medivh players believe Medivh to be the rightful victor and take pride in the cooperation and organization demonstrated on their server.\r\n===Guilds===\r\n====IRC====\r\n'''Network:''' Stratics\r\n'''Servers:''' irc.stratics.com:6668, irc.glowfish.de:7000\r\n'''Channels:''' #Ascent, #Fury, #Godspeed",},
			["Server:Moonglade Europe"] = { content = "==History of Moonglade (Europe)==\r\nWhilst all realms share one common storyline and history, they all deviate slightly because of player created storylines and content. Every single realm is technically an alternative world, and the timeline whilst having key points (eg. Blizzard-created events) still has unique Player-created events, stories and adventures that only exist in the one timeline. This makes each realm special in it's own right, and Moonglade is no exception.\r\n===Historical Events in Moonglade===\r\nThere were many events in Moonglade over the years, some of which are listed below.\r\n====Steamwheedle Faire====\r\nConsidered to be the largest organised roleplaying event in the history of the Moonglade realm, over 250 people attended in total, almost causing the server that hosts the Tanaris region to crash.\r\nDespite the sheer size and logistical problems presented by catering for both Horde and Alliance, the Faire was a resounding success and there was practically no trouble.\r\nKaboom gave away free ale, hosted a raffle for a free pet for both the Horde and Alliance attendees, a storytelling contest and a boxing match.\r\nThe event lasted from approximately 16:00 until 19:00 and saw people queueing, dancing, sun bathing and having a good time in [[Steamwheedle Port]] a relatively untravelled location.\r\n====Steamwheedle Faire 2====\r\nA follow up to the Original fair, this was organised by House Idrial, The Torchlight Outpost, The Mithril Guard, The Outriders and Rhyme & Punishment. Though not as large as the original fair, there were more events, more prizes and more free drinks than the original, and the fair lasted many hours. Among the highlights of the fair were a display piece presented by the Mithril Guard, and a poetry competition. The event was only slightly marred by a sandstorm.\r\n====The Old Town Fair====\r\nOn Tuesday, October 9th 2007 an Old Town Fair encouraged the Stormwind citizens to remember the less fortunate merchants of the [[Old Town]] district and to help out the poor and needy.\r\nThe Mithril Guard started off with a parade to gather all participants for the speech of the Baron of . Afterwards, crafters and vendors from different houses and guilds (many members of the Zanadu RP-community) presented their merchandise, under the watchful eyes of the city guard.\r\nThere were barbecue stands, free drinks, surprise boxes, a race and a lottery that granted one lucky winner 500 gold. The event lasted from approximately 20:00 until 22:00.\r\n====The Opening of Ahn'Qiraj====\r\nThe quest chain to open the Gates of [[Ahn'Qiraj]] was successfully completed on Moonglade by '''Vir Mortalis''', an Alliance based raiding guild. The event began on a Sunday morning at 7am and took ten hours to complete. During the opening event and the Eranikus event in Moonglade, Vir Mortalis was assisted by the Horde guild '''Honorbound.'''\r\nVir Mortalis came under fire at the time from various sources for \"not informing the rest of the realm,\" that the Gates would be opened on this day at the time specified. argued that this was to prevent server crashes and because they had put the majority of the effort into completing the ''epic'' quest.\r\n====A Day at the Races====\r\nFalcore of '''Rhyme and Punishment''' organised for a collection of community photographs to be created on Sunday, 10th September 2006. The event was a huge success with over one hundred people from both the [[Horde]] and the [[Alliance]] attending at it's peak.\r\nMany screenshots (aka. photographs) were taken, and a very positive community atmosphere was felt by everyone who attended, new or adept. It has been proposed that such an event should take a yearly slot in the calendar.\r\n====The Silvermoon Charity Ball====\r\nThe May 19th 2007 saw the Horde amassing for a charity ball set amidst the elegant spires of Silvermoon City. The ball was organised by Narihka and her Blood Guard guild and proved to be an enormous success.\r\nThe ball played host to many different representatives from a multitude of different guilds who received a special introduction prior to the beginning of the event. The hall was thronged with guests enjoying the food and drink supplied by the catering staff, dancing, conversing and simply taking full advantage of the festive atmosphere.\r\n====The Tranquilien Assault====\r\nOn the 20th of March 2008, an RP world PvP event took place in the Ghostlands. The attack was announced on the realm forum by Nairuil of the Circle of VIdomi and organized on both sides making it in a sense a cross faction event. About 25 members of the Alliance, all over level 60, joined. Resistance was put up by Armos of the Boldblood Clan.\r\n====The Battle of Theramore====\r\nA [[roleplay]] event on [[Server:Moonglade Europe|Moonglade EU]] depicting the reign of [[User:Cierran/Highlord|Highlord]] [[Server:Moonglade EU/Tristam|Tristam Galahand]] and the rise and fall of his son, [[Server:Moonglade EU/Melkorius|Melkorius Galahand]], based around [[Theramore Isle]]. The event was kickstarted by the [[Guild:Regiment of Theramore (Moonglade EU)|Regiment of Theramore]] to bring RP to such an empty city.\r\n===Moonglade Roleplaying Communities===\r\nTo encourage a realm-wide community and help foster a good roleplaying environment, roleplaying communities have been established on both factions.\r\nCurrently, the following roleplaying communities are established and fully operational on Moonglade:\r\n* \r\nAn Alliance based community. Players are encouraged to join as part of their RP based guild, not as individuals, wherever possible. The Zanadu channel is to encourage RP storylines, events, discussion and promotion across the server. The Zanadu project also has a smaller subset of people active in promoting RP based raids, covering both old and new raid content.\r\n* The SquareRP community is no longer under active development, and most members have now moved on to other projects (such as Zanadu). The channel still exists but is barely active, and the website is no longer accessible.\r\nThe Moonglade Adventurer's and Roleplayer's community is a Horde based organisation that attempts to establish RP reasons for End Game raiding. It has proven to be very successful and popular.\r\nIs a Horde based RP community. The members see themselves to be the \"true\" [[Shadow Council]] and see all members of the in-game NPC faction The [[Shadow Council]] to be enslaved weaklings and fools. They want the Horde to return to the old ways and think that all attempts to peace with the Alliance are foolhearty.\r\n Is a RP Guild Pact based in [[Silvermoon]]. The Council mainly RP that they are a advisor Council of the Lord Regent. Their mission is to lead their fellow blood elves from survival to glory.\r\nSeveral other communities have been proposed in the past, including one based on the Island of [[Theramore]] called , as well as communities based in [[Lakeshire]], [[Darnassus]] and [[Southshore]]. Hopefully in the future, such endevours will prove to be successful.\r\n===News Sources and Entertainment===\r\n* \r\n Currently active and producing new content\r\n===Other Role-playing Resources===\r\n* \r\n* \r\n* \r\n* \r\n*",},
			["Server:Ner'zhul US"] = { content = "*'''Realm''' = Ner'zhul\r\n*'''Region''' = US\r\n*'''Battlegroup''' = Bloodlust\r\n*'''Category''' = [[PvP]]\r\n*'''Time-Zone''' = Pacific US\r\n*'''Population''' = ~21,000 Level 10-70 Characters (As reported by WarcraftRealms.com 07-07-2007)\r\n*'''Factions''' = [[Alliance]] = ~9,600 Level 10-70 Characters, [[Horde]] = ~11,500 Level 10-70 Characters\r\n*'''Status''' = Deployed as of 12-31-2004\r\n==Summary==\r\nNer'zhul is a legacy server and one of the originally deployed servers at the premiere of World of Warcraft. Because of this, the server had a history of hardware problems resulting in occasional server restarts several times a weekly cycle. Once Blizzard updated the server hardware around the release of [[The Burning Crusade]] Expansion, most problems were resolved and the server now accommodates thousands of players with a concentration on Pacific-zoned regions. The server is well populated and established, and is home to several high end guilds advancing through cutting edge content. Ner'zhul is a [[PvP]] server, and is also home to several elite PvP groups and [[Arena Teams]] in the Bloodlust battlegroup. Horde and Alliance tend to dominant PvP more or less on equal terms, however Alliance hold a significant lead in PvE endeavors. The most progressed PvE Guild is Strictly Business. The most widely known individuals are WoW TCG Lead Developer Elendril and longtime infamous PvP Rogue Tyrrana. Wet Dreams, Vicious Cycle, WHY DID WE BRING A DRUID, and Not Even Good were all Top 10 5v5 [[Arena Teams]] in Arena Season 1.\r\n==Notable Points==\r\n*Ner'zhul was one of servers made famous by a collaboration of a few crazed individuals who managed to pull [[Lord Kazzak]] from his base in Blasted Lands to wreck havoc on the Alliance city Stormwind. \r\n*While officially designated a PST server, a number of Oceanic guilds reside on Ner'zhul and actively conduct raids at off-peak times relative to North American players.\r\n*A highly regarded [[Gnome]] [[rogue]] named Walle was challenged to a series of duels by the [[Tauren]] [[shaman]] Gweldoc of Shadow Gypsies. Gweldoc had created a thread on the US Ner'zhul forums brazenly declaring his superiority to Walle in that he would be ''\"riding you up and down Azeroth without the use of interface mods, health potions, or tubers.\"'' Gweldoc would then chronicle his feats in his self-proclaimed upcoming video Wheres Walle. Shortly after word of this surfaced, Walle produced a video in response... .\r\n*All three pre-TBC [[Alliance]] cities of [[Azeroth]] ([[Darnassus]], [[Ironforge]], [[Stormwind]]) have had their leaders assassinated at least once by [[Horde]] players. The Alliance have also returned the favor by killing at least once the leader of [[Thunder Bluff]] and [[Orgrimmar]].\r\n*The server is also the home of the original [[Kralnor]], the patron saint of all warlocks.\r\n==Server Precedents==\r\n'''[[Black Temple]]'''\r\n*First Attuned: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance -- 06/22/07\r\n*High Warlord Naj'entus: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance -- 07/02/07\r\n*Supremus: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance -- 07/02/07\r\n*Shade of Akama: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance -- 07/02/07\r\n*Teron Gorefiend: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance -- 07/09/07\r\n*Gurtogg Bloodboil: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance -- 08/09/07\r\n*Reliquary of Souls: Strictly Business -- Alliance -- 08/24/07\r\n*Mother Shahraz: Strictly Business -- Alliance -- 9/13/07\r\n*Illidari Council: Strictly Business -- Alliance -- 9/14/07\r\n*Illidan Stormrage: Strictly Business -- Alliance -- 9/20/07\r\n'''[[Battle for Mount Hyjal]]'''\r\n*First Attuned: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance -- 06/19/07\r\n*Rage Winterchill: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance -- 06/22/07\r\n*Anetheron: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance -- 06/24/07\r\n*Kaz'rogal: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance -- 07/05/07\r\n*Azgalor: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance -- 07/11/07\r\n*Archimonde: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance -- 08/09/07\r\n'''[[Eye (Tempest Keep)]]'''\r\n*Al'ar: Lost Anarchy -- 06/04/07\r\n*Void Reaver: Strictly Business -- Alliance -- 04/13/07\r\n*High Astromancer Solarian: Strictly Business -- Alliance -- 06/06/07\r\n*Kael'thas Sunstrider: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance -- 06/19/07\r\n'''[[Serpentshrine Cavern]]'''\r\n*Hydross the Unstable: Alliance\r\n*The Lurker Below : Strictly Business -- Alliance -- 05/08/07\r\n*Leotheras the Blind: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance -- \r\n*Fathom-Lord Karathress: Alliance\r\n*Morogrim Tidewalker: Alliance\r\n*Lady Vashj: Strictly Business -- Alliance -- 05/28/07\r\n'''[[Magtheridon's Lair]]'''\r\n*Magtheridon: Lost Anarchy -- Alliance --\r\n==PvE Guild Rankings==\r\n[Guild] -- [Faction] -- [Bosses killed from TK, Hyjal, BT --> Max of 18]\r\n--\r\nRankings calculated by Blizzaron based upon information reported by stickied thread on WoW US Ner'zhul Forums.\r\n'''Tier 1'''\r\n* -- Alliance - 18\r\n* -- Horde -- 18\r\n* -- Alliance -- 18\r\n'''Tier 2'''\r\n* -- Alliance -- 14\r\n*Virulent -- Alliance -- 12\r\n*Lemmings -- Horde -- 11\r\n'''Tier 3'''\r\n*Bahamut -- Horde -- 9\r\n*Horde Yakka -- Horde -- 7\r\n*Vendetta -- Alliance -- 3\r\n*Dissonance -- Alliance -- 3\r\n*Local Defense -- Alliance -- 3\r\n*Disengaged -- Alliance -- 3\r\n*Spike Flail -- Horde -- 2\r\n*Disengaged -- Alliance -- 2\r\n'''Tier 4'''\r\n* -- Horde -- 1\r\n*dinosaur -- Alliance -- 1\r\n*Happy Ending -- Horde -- 1\r\n*Dissent -- Horde -- 1\r\n*Peter Had Jumper Cables -- Horde -- 1\r\n*Disciples of Death -- Alliance -- 1\r\n*Last Call -- Horde -- 1\r\n*Carnage -- Alliance -- 1\r\n*Dishonorable -- Alliance -- 1\r\n*Ghost -- Alliance -- 1\r\n*Blind Leading the Blind & orz -- Horde -- 1\r\n*Defiance -- Horde -- 1\r\n*CheeR -- Alliance -- 1\r\n*DietCokeTin -- Alliance -- 1\r\n*Jolly Rogers -- Alliance -- 1\r\n*AoS -- Alliance -- 1\r\n*Shadow Prophecy -- Alliance -- 1\r\n--\r\n*Note: SSC has been excluded from rank determination in order to keep list more concise and concentrated.\r\n*Individual guild rankings may be updated daily, complete rankings updated weekly.\r\n*Updated 10/11/07 by Bramble\r\n==PvE Server Rankings (Bloodlust Battlegroup)==\r\n''Updated periodically (1-2 weeks), this list shows the furthest each server is on the Bloodlust Battlegroup in raid progression.''\r\n*Number represents each unique boss killed in TK, Hyjal, and BT. Total = 18\r\n*Information taken from .\r\n*Edited on 09/23/07 by Bramble.\r\n'''Tier 1'''\r\n* -- PvP -- 18\r\n* -- PvP -- 18\r\n* -- PvE -- 18\r\n* -- PvP -- 18\r\n* -- PvE -- 18\r\n* -- PvP -- 18\r\n* -- PvP -- 18\r\n* -- PvE -- 18\r\n* -- PvP -- 18\r\n'''Tier 2'''\r\n* -- PvE -- 17\r\n* -- PvP -- 15\r\n* -- PvE -- 15\r\n* -- PvE -- 14\r\n* -- PvE -- 14\r\n'''Tier 3'''\r\n* -- PvP -- 10\r\n* -- PvE -- 9\r\n'''Tier 4'''\r\n* -- RP -- 3\r\n'''Notes:'''\r\n*Kil'jaedan boasts the first two guilds with full completion of current raiding content.\r\n*The lowest ranked server is the only [[RP]] server.\r\n==PvP Rankings==\r\n''For most up-to-date information please reference :''\r\n*\r\n==Server Professionals -- Alchemy==\r\n* [[Destruction Potion]] -- Hyetei(A), Quidamtyra(A), Utada(A), Prea(H), Talfryn(H), Antiquitus(H)\r\n* [[Elixir of Major Mageblood]] -- Kondara(A), Samantha(A), Hyetei(A), Hoshichan(A), Aeterna(A)\r\n* [[Elixir of Major Shadow Power]] -- Xwright(A), Kondara(A), Paulter(A), Utada(A), Quidamtyra(A), Holycoronas(A), Aeterna(A), Dezian(H), Prea(H), Talfryn(H)\r\n* [[Elixir of the Searching Eye]] -- Utada(A), Xwright(A), Quidamtyra(A), Prea(H)\r\n* [[Fel Mana Potion]] -- Kondara(A), Paulter(A), Hyetei(A), Bloopy(A), Utada(A), Quidamtyra(A), Holycoronas(A), Aeterna(A), Prea(H), Dezian(H), Kenai(H), Talfryn(H) \r\n* [[Fel Regeneration Potion]] -- Magicoronas(A), Quidamtyra(A), Utada(A), Xwright(A), Dezian(H), Prea(H), Talfryn(H)\r\n* [[Fel Strength Elixir]] -- Kondara(A), Paulter(A), Hyetei(A), Bloopy(A), Quidamtyra(A), Aeterna(A), Utada(A), Prea(H), Dezian(H), Kenai(H), Talfryn(H)\r\n* [[Flask of Arcane Fortification]] -- Kondara(A), Utada(A), Chunder(A), Koho(H), Antiquitus(H)\r\n* [[Flask of Fortification]] -- Julie(A), Gatsbee(A), Utada(A), Quidamtyra(A), Koho(H), Antiquitus(H)\r\n* [[Flask of Mighty Restoration]] -- Kondara(A), Fally(A), Utada (A), Stormrain(A), Quidamtyra(A), Prea(H), Antiquitus(H), Kiona(A), Akamaru(A), Doboy(A)\r\n* [[Flask of Relentless Assault]] -- Gatsbee(A), Holycoronas(A), Igniter(A), Kondara(A), Magicoronas(A), Paulter(A), Utada(A), Damiens(H), Kenai(H), Prea(H), Talfryn(H), Antiquitus(H)\r\n* [[Flask of Shadow Fortification]] -- Kondara(A), Damiens(H), Dezian(H), Talfryn(H), Antiquitus(H)\r\n* [[Haste Potion]] -- Hyetei(A), Quidamtyra(A), Talfryn(H), Antiquitus(H)\r\n* [[Heroic Potion]] -- Gatsbee(A), Quidamtyra(A), Xwright(A)\r\n* [[Insane Strength Potion]] -- Gatsbee(A), Bloopy(A), Utada(A), Quidamtyra(A), Talfryn(H)\r\n* [[Ironshield Potion]] -- Julie(A), Potatoofdoom(A), Bloopy(A), Quidamtyra(A), Utada(A), Holycoronas(A), Aeterna(A), Chunder(A), Prea(H)\r\n* [[Major Arcane Protection Potion]] -- Potatoofdoom(A), Hyetei(A), Gatsbee(A), Utada(A), Quidamtyra(A), Prea(H), Dezian(H), Talfryn(H) \r\n* [[Major Fire Protection Potion]] -- Fally(A), Holycoronas(A), Aeterna(A)\r\n* [[Major Frost Protection Potion]] -- Utada(A), Aeterna(A)\r\n* [[Major Holy Protection Potion]] -- Potatoofdoom(A), Hyetei(A), Utada(A), Prea(H)\r\n* [[Major Nature Protection Potion]] -- Hyetei(A), Utada(A), Holycoronas(A), Aeterna(A), Quidamtyra(A), Dezian(H)\r\n* [[Major Shadow Protection Potion]] -- Potatoofdoom(A), Hyetei(A), Gatsbee(A), Utada(A), Aeterna(A), Prea(H), Dezian(H), Talryn(H)\r\n* [[Super Rejuvenation Potion]] -- Quidamtyra(A), Chunder(A), Kenai(H), Antiquitus(H)\r\n==Server Professionals -- Blacksmithing==\r\n'''Armor'''\r\n* [[Black Felsteel Bracers]] -- Soulrazor(A), Bigbatista(A)\r\n* [[Blessed Bracers]] -- Daenaria(A), Davey(A), Damiens(H), Soulrazor(A), Herlucia (A),Bigbatista(A)\r\n* [[Bracers of the Green Fortress]] -- Triton(A), Herlucia (A),Bigbatista(A)\r\n* [[Earthpeace Breastplate]] -- Hella(A), Cherlize(A), Davey(A), Mithwrath(H)\r\n* [[Felfury Gauntlets]] -- Jibbs(A), Ruleofwrist(A), Mithwrath(H),Bigbatista(A)\r\n* [[Felsteel Gloves]] -- Cherlize(A),Bigbatista(A)\r\n* [[Felsteel Helm]] -- Jibbs(A), Ruleofwrist(A), Cherlize(A), Davey(A), Berius(A), Orinoko(H), Schrecken(H), Mithwrath(H), Soulrazor(A)\r\n* [[Felsteel Leggings]] -- Hella(A), Ruleofwrist(A), Davey(A), Mithwrath(H)\r\n* [[Khorium Belt]] -- Triton(A), Cherlize(A), Schrecken(H), Soulrazor(A)\r\n* [[Khorium Boots]] -- Jibbs(A), Triton(A), Soulrazor(A)\r\n* [[Khorium Pants]] -- Triton(A), Cherlize(A), Davey(A), Schrecken(H), Soulrazor(A)\r\n* [[Oathkeeper's Helm]] -- Hella(A), Herlucia (A),Bigbatista(A)\r\n* [[Ragesteel Breastplate]] -- Triton(A), Dizoliti(A), Soulrazor(A)\r\n* [[Ragesteel Gloves]] -- Triton(A), Dizoliti(A), Swallowed(A), Herlucia(A), Soulrazor(A)\r\n* [[Ragesteel Helm]] -- Triton(A), Dizoliti(A)\r\n* [[Ragesteel Shoulders]] -- Soulrazor(A)\r\n* [[Steelgrip Gauntlets]] -- Triton(A), Tawook(A)\r\n* [[Storm Helm]] -- Ruleofwrist(A), Dizoliti(A), Urayan(H), Herlucia (A)\r\n* [[Swiftsteel Gloves]] -- Ruleofwrist(A), Dizoliti(A), Soulrazor(A)\r\n* [[Helm of the Stalwart Defender]] -- Soulrazor(A), Herlucia (A),Bigbatista(A)\r\n* [[Belt of the Guardian]] -- Soulrazor(A),Bigbatista(A)\r\n* [[Red Belt of Battle]] -- Hashut(A)\r\n----\r\n'''Weapons'''\r\n* [[Dirge]] -- Soulrazor(A) Swallowed(A), Berius(A), \r\n* [[Eternium Runed Blade]] -- Cherlize(A), Kurency(A)\r\n* [[Fel Edged Battleaxe]] -- Cherlize(A), Berius(A), Mithwrath(H)\r\n* [[Fel Hardened Maul]] -- Soulrazor(A), Ruleofwrist(A), Herlucia (A)\r\n* [[Felsteel Longblade]] -- Cherlize(A), Dizoliti(A), Kurency(A), Conky(H), Herlucia (A),Bigbatista(A)\r\n* [[Felsteel Reaper]] -- Blkscorpion(H)\r\n* [[Hand of Eternity]] -- Soulrazor(A), Cherlize(A),Bigbatista(A)\r\n* [[Khorium Champion]] -- Bananars(H), Herlucia (A)\r\n* [[Runic Hammer]] -- Soulrazor(A), Berius(A), Seraphan(H), Herlucia (A)\r\n==Server Professionals -- Enchanting==\r\n* [[E