			["Category:Transportation"] = { content = "Transportation encompasses the various means on traveling around in [[World of Warcraft]].\r\nSee also:\r\n* [[Travel Guide]]\r\n* The excellent at .\r\n= Basic =\r\n==Walking/Running==\r\nRunning is the main method of exploring the world. Flight paths require you to run to their Flight Masters around the world to unlock them. Teleports, Portals, Boats, Zeppelins, and the Deeprun Tram only have set destinations. [[Transportation|Mounts]] are a form of running.\r\nSeveral classes gain a [[power]] to increase their run speed.\r\n*[[Hunter]]s have [[Aspect of the Cheetah]] (lvl 20) and [[Aspect of the Pack]] (lvl 40).\r\n*[[Druid]]s have a [[Travel Form]] trainable at level 30. Also, talent points can be invested to increase running speed in cat form by 15% per each of two points for this talent in the Feral tree. This 15% bonus to cat form movement speed, as well as a set bonus from the pvp rare set, can make travel in cat form faster than in travel form itself.\r\n*[[Shaman]]s have a [[Ghost Wolf|Ghost Wolf Form]], trainable at level 20.\r\n*[[Mage]]s do not have a constant speed boosting skill, however at level 20 they may periodically use \"[[blink]]\" in order to shorten their travel time.\r\n*[[Rogue]]s have an ability called [[Sprint]], which increases running speed by 50-70% depending on level, and does stack with the Minor Speed Increase enchant. This ability can be used while stealthed and doesn't break stealth. This ability also makes the Rogue a successful flag carrier in [[Warsong Gulch]]. However, this effect only lasts 15 seconds, and is limited by a 5-minute cooldown. This ability is therefore best left for an quick getaway, to sneak up quickly while stealthed, or to catch a zeppelin/boat before it leaves.\r\n*[[Paladin]]s have the [[Pursuit of Justice]] talent, which increases their normal and mounted movement speed by 4% per talent point invested (up to 8%). Unfortunately, this does not stack with mithril spurs, carrot on a stick, or the riding speed enchant.\r\n* [[Warrior]]s can charge at an enemy, then [[hamstring]] and run away.\r\n==Swimming==\r\nSwimming is, by far, the slowest way of getting anywhere, since it subtracts your speed by 50% and speed buffs do not work while swimming, save for one alchemy potion. It can also be dangerous, as you have a [[breath]] meter while underwater, and if you go deep enough (meaning far enough away from land), a [[fatigue]] meter. When a [[breath]] or [[fatigue]] meter reaches 0, the player takes damage every few seconds, until they surface or leave the high pressure area. \r\n[[Druid]]s have an [[Aquatic Form]] that protects them from drowning, and increases their swimming speed by 100%, raising their swim speed to be level with normal run speed. In addition, [[Warlock]] and [[Shaman]] spells and Elixirs of (Greater) Water Breathing allow you to breathe underwater, and [[Shaman]]s and [[Priest]]s may also cast a spell to allows them to walk on water. [[Forsaken]] have a racial ability which helps them last longer underwater, increasing their breath by 300%. In addition, [[engineer]]s at level 230 can create [[Deepdive Helmet]]s to breath permanently underwater.\r\nThere is also a trinket called Hook of the Master Angler, one of the prizes for being the winner in the Stranglethorn Fishing Contest. It turns the user into a fish, increasing their swim speed by 100% as well as allowing underwater breath, though the effect cancels upon strike, which in a sense makes druid aquatic form more desirable in some scenarios.\r\n=Rapid-Transit ([[Flight Paths]])=\r\n===[[Zeppelin]]===\r\n=Inter-Continental=\r\n===[[Boat]]===\r\n* [[Ratchet]], [[The Barrens]] &harr; [[Booty Bay]], [[Stranglethorn Vale]]\r\n* [[Menethil Harbor]], [[Wetlands]] &harr; [[Theramore Isle]], [[Dustwallow Marsh]]\r\n* [[Menethil Harbor]], [[Wetlands]] &harr; [[Auberdine]], [[Darkshore]]\r\n* [[Rut'theran Village]], [[Teldrassil]] &harr; [[Auberdine]], [[Darkshore]]\r\n* The [[Forgotten Coast]], [[Feralas]] &harr; [[Feathermoon Stronghold]], [[Feralas]]\r\n===[[Zeppelin]]===\r\n* [[Orgrimmar]], [[Durotar]] &harr; [[Grom'Gol]], [[Stranglethorn Vale]]\r\n* [[Orgrimmar]], [[Durotar]] &harr; [[Undercity]], [[Tirisfal Glades]]\r\n* [[Undercity]], [[Tirisfal Glades]] &harr; [[Grom'Gol]], [[Stranglethorn Vale]]\r\n=[[Mounts]]=\r\n===[[Orc]] - [[Wolf]]===\r\n* Dire Wolf\r\n* Timber Wolf\r\n* Brown Wolf\r\n* Swift Brown Wolf (Epic)\r\n* Swift Timber Wolf (Epic)\r\n* Swift Gray Wolf (Epic)\r\n===[[Tauren]] - [[Kodo]]===\r\n* Gray Kodo\r\n* Brown Kodo\r\n* Green Kodo (Old Epic, No longer available)\r\n* Teal Kodo (Old Epic, No longer available)\r\n* Great White Kodo (Epic)\r\n* Great Grey Kodo (Epic)\r\n* Great Brown Kodo (Epic)\r\n===[[Forsaken]] - [[Skeletal Horse]]===\r\n* Blue Skeletal Horse\r\n* Brown Skeletal Horse\r\n* Red Skeletal Horse\r\n* Green Skeletal Warhorse (Epic)\r\n* Purple Skeletal Warhorse (Epic)\r\n===[[Troll]] - [[Raptor]]===\r\n* Emerald Raptor\r\n* Turquoise Raptor\r\n* Violet Raptor\r\n* Mottled Red Raptor (Old Epic, No longer available)\r\n* Ivory Raptor (Old Epic, No longer available)\r\n* Swift Olive Raptor (Epic)\r\n* Swift Orange Raptor (Epic)\r\n* Swift Blue Raptor (Epic)\r\n===[[Blood Elf]] - [[Hawkstrider]]===\r\n*Not yet implemented\r\n===[[Human]] - [[Horse]]===\r\n* Black Stallion\r\n* Brown Horse\r\n* Chestnut Mare\r\n* Pinto\r\n* Swift Palomino (Epic)\r\n* Swift White Steed (Epic)\r\n* Swift Brown Steed (Epic)\r\n===[[Night Elf]] - [[Nightsaber]]===\r\n* Striped Nightsaber\r\n* Spotted Frostsaber\r\n* Striped Frostsaber\r\n* Swift Stormsaber (Epic)\r\n* Swift Frostsaber (Epic)\r\n* Swift Mistsaber (Epic)\r\n* Winterspring Frostsaber (Epic)\r\n===[[Gnome]] - [[Mechanostrider]]===\r\n* Blue Mechanostrider\r\n* Green Mechanostrider\r\n* Red Mechanostrider\r\n* Unpainted Mechanostrider\r\n* Swift Green Mechanostrider (Epic)\r\n* Swift Yellow Mechanostrider (Epic)\r\n* Swift White Mechanostrider (Epic)\r\n===[[Dwarf]] - [[Ram]]===\r\n* Brown Ram\r\n* White Ram\r\n* Gray Ram\r\n* Swift Gray Ram (Epic)\r\n* Swift Brown Ram (Epic)\r\n* Swift White Ram (Epic)\r\n===[[Draenei]] - [[Elekk]]===\r\n*Not yet implemented\r\n==[[Paladin]]==\r\n* Warhorse\r\n* Charger (Epic)\r\n==[[Warlock]]==\r\n* Felsteed\r\n* Dreadsteed (Epic)\r\n==Rare/Other==\r\n* '''Swift Razzashi Raptor''' - An epic mount that randomly drops in the [[Zul'Gurub]] instance.\r\n* '''Swift Zulian Tiger''' - An epic mount that randomly drops in the [[Zul'Gurub]] instance.\r\n* '''Deathcharger''' - The mount of [[Baron Rivendare]].\r\n* '''Ravasaurs''' - Raptors native to [[Un'Goro Crater]].\r\n===[[Ahn'Qiraj]]===\r\nThe [[Ahn'Qiraj]] instance (released in patch 1.9) features several large insectoid mounts available for players to ride through the large expanses of the instance, since it was the largest in the game upon its implementation. These include blue, green, red, and yellow varieties. There is also a black variety, only obtainable to the person who rings the Scarab Gong to start the Ahn'Qiraj world event, that allows it's owner to use it anywhere, not just the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj.\r\n===Horde===\r\n* '''Frostwolf Howler''' - Available for purchase at the [[Frostwolf]] Clan of [[Alterac Valley]]. (Requires level 60)\r\n* '''Black War Wolf''' - Requires level 40*\r\n* '''Black War Raptor''' - Requires level 40\r\n* '''Black War Kodo''' - Requires level 40\r\n* '''Red Skeletal Warhorse''' - Requires level 40\r\n===Alliance===\r\n* '''Stormpike Riding Ram''' - Available for purchase after reaching Exalted status with the [[Stormpike]] clan of [[Alterac Valley]]. (Requires level 60)\r\n* '''Black Warsteed''' - Requires level 40*\r\n* '''Black Battle Ram''' - Requires level 40\r\n* '''Black Battlestrider''' - Requires level 40\r\n* '''Black War Tiger''' - Requires level 40 and Honor\r\n= Teleportation =\r\n==Death==\r\nUpon dying, your character will be teleported to the nearest graveyard. You can either run back to your body and choose a place to resurrect near there, or ask the [[Spirit Healer]] to resurrect you at the graveyard.\r\n==[[Hearthstone]]==\r\n* Can be used once every hour to transport the player to their home location.\r\n==[[Dark Portal|The Dark Portal]]==\r\n* Leads to [[Outland]].\r\n* Must first be opened through an in-game event upon release of the [[Burning Crusade]] expansion.\r\n==[[Mage]] [[Portal]]==\r\n* Mages can create a portal to the [[capital]] city of their choosing, with the proper spell. The mage has two versions of this: a self-only [[Teleport]] and a [[Portal]] for group members.\r\n==[[Teleport: Moonglade]]==\r\n* Similar to a Mage's self-only [[Teleport]], this allows a [[Druid]] to teleport to [[Moonglade]].\r\n==[[Ritual of Summoning]]==\r\n* [[Warlock]]s can cast this spell to transport a [[party]] member to them.\r\n* Requires at least 4 party members - a Warlock to initiate the ritual, 2 others nearby to participate in the ritual, and 1 to be transported to the rest of the party.\r\n* Requires a soul shard reagent, which the warlock can aquire through the soul drain spell.\r\n==[[Astral Recall]]==\r\n* Allows a [[Shaman]] to transport to their home location.\r\n* Basically, it's a [[Hearthstone]] you can use every 15 minutes and doesn't requre a bag slot.\r\n==[[Transporter]]==\r\n* See [[Transporter]]s for more info.\r\n===Telepolyporter 3000===\r\n*Allows [[Horde]] players to transport from [[Booty Bay]] to [[Gnomeregan]], and vice versa.\r\n===Ultrasafe Transporter===\r\n*Gnomish [[Engineer]]s with 260 skill can create a gizmo that will transport them to [[Gadgetzan]].\r\n*4-hour cooldown.\r\n*Some side-effects may occur, and include:\r\n** Missing the destination transporter pad and appearing several hundred feet away, high above the desert. The fall will probably kill you, and will cause 10% durability loss to your gear. Have a [[Parachute Cloak]] equipped and be ready to activate it.\r\n** The creation of an \"evil twin\".\r\n** Being transformed into a [[Trogg]] for a short period of time.\r\n===Dimensional Ripper===\r\n*Goblin [[Engineer]]s with 260 skill can create a gizmo that will transport them to [[Everlook]].\r\n*4-hour cooldown.\r\n*Some side-effects may occur, and include:\r\n** Catching fire and dying when you appear in Everlook.",},
